{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052686-garou-and-vampires","id":1052686,"title":"Garou and Vampires","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-02-21T12:19:26-08:00","id":1052686,"title":"Garou and Vampires","content":"I checked W20 corebook and for me, it's disappointing. Why Garou still hate vampires? I mean, vampires definitelyare not lovely creatures in the world... but neither Garou. And now, this dump hate seems to be so hypocritical and fanatic. The only adequate reason for Gaou to hate vampires is Wyrm smell - and why not to retcon all this 'all vampires smell like Wyrm'? Why both factions couldn't have some kind of passive-histile neutrality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T12:34:14-08:00","id":1052696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052686-garou-and-vampires#post1052686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I checked W20 corebook and for me, it's disappointing. Why Garou still hate vampires? I mean, vampires definitelyare not lovely creatures in the world... but neither Garou. And now, this dump hate seems to be so hypocritical and fanatic. The only adequate reason for Gaou to hate vampires is Wyrm smell - and why not to retcon all this 'all vampires smell like Wyrm'? Why both factions couldn't have some kind of passive-histile neutrality.</div> </div> </div> </div>All Vampires of Humanity 6 or lower stink of the Wyrm. This means that Changing Breeds interact with the worst of Vampires, since the good Vampires are kind of invisible to them almost. I doubt most Werewolves even know that high Humanity Vampires exist.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, Vampires have Presence and Dominate. Growing up, pups will be told to not even speak to Vampires, one look and you'll be their slave. They have plenty of reason to hate and fear them, and visa versa.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T12:37:29-08:00","id":1052698,"title":"","content":"Nosferatu and Bone Gnawers have a working relationship.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T13:05:13-08:00","id":1052715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Furthermore, Vampires have Presence and Dominate </div> </div> </div>Yep<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I doubt most Werewolves even know that high Humanity Vampires exist. </div> </div> </div> Although they would most probably kill even high-Humanity vampires, if they would know that this is vampire.<br /> It's anyway sounds. Why vampire must smell like Wyrm, first of all? It doesn't add anything to crossover. Here they sound kind of supernatural Nazi:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For millennia, werewolves and vampires have fought<br /> bloody wars throughout the world. Werewolves typically<br /> feel that the only good Leech is a Leech that\u2019s been burned<br /> to ashes and scattered to the four winds. Whereas most<br /> Garou prefer the open wilderness, vampires are creatures<br /> of the city. They survive and thrive on human blood, and<br /> they could not survive in the wilderness even without the<br /> werewolves\u2019 crushing their every intrusion. Many Garou<br /> blame vampires for the unchecked invasion of urban centers<br /> deeper and deeper into previously untamed wilderness. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T13:17:14-08:00","id":1052722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052686-garou-and-vampires?p=1052715#post1052715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yep<br /> Although they would most probably kill even high-Humanity vampires, if they would know that this is vampire.<br /> It's anyway sounds. Why vampire must smell like Wyrm, first of all? It doesn't add anything to crossover. Here they sound kind of supernatural Nazi:</div> </div> </div> </div>Vampires in Golconda are left alone by Werewolves and the like. And some Garou are on &quot;you don't kill me I don't kill you&quot; terms with Werewolves.<br /> <br /> Vampires smell like the Wyrm because they are creatures perpetually caught in their moment of death. That's what Vampires are, scientifically and spiritually. They died, but their death is extended to infinity and they are held in that stasis forever. This makes them simultaneously wracked with Weaver and Wyrmish influence. The Garou just smell the stench of the Wyrm.<br /> <br /> The mutual antagonism exists for a tonne of reasons, and then feeds off of itself. Reconciling the two groups is nearly impossible. Keep in mind that the interests of Vampires line up quite neatly with Pentex and the Technocracy in some cases. If a Ventrue Prince is a billionaire, a good portion of his portfolio is tied to Pentex or the Syndicate (whether they know it or not; these businesses are just the best performers on paper and will be something the Ventrue, Lasombra and Giovanni (among others) buy into), and that makes them complicit in the war on the Garou Nation and other Fera. And Vampires are the masters of cities and governments, and therefore Werewolves can easily blame them for pollution and polluting policies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T13:38:47-08:00","id":1052733,"title":"","content":"Camarilla Kindred can develop cordial working relationships with Garou if they work through the proper intermediaries, but Garou and Kindred are never going to become allies unless there is a bigger threat to both groups than each other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T13:39:50-08:00","id":1052734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052686-garou-and-vampires?p=1052722#post1052722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Vampires in Golconda are left alone by Werewolves and the like. And some Garou are on &quot;you don't kill me I don't kill you&quot; terms with Werewolves.<br /> <br /> Vampires smell like the Wyrm because they are creatures perpetually caught in their moment of death. That's what Vampires are, scientifically and spiritually. They died, but their death is extended to infinity and they are held in that stasis forever. This makes them simultaneously wracked with Weaver and Wyrmish influence. The Garou just smell the stench of the Wyrm.<br /> <br /> The mutual antagonism exists for a tonne of reasons, and then feeds off of itself. Reconciling the two groups is nearly impossible. Keep in mind that the interests of Vampires line up quite neatly with Pentex and the Technocracy in some cases. If a Ventrue Prince is a billionaire, a good portion of his portfolio is tied to Pentex or the Syndicate (whether they know it or not; these businesses are just the best performers on paper and will be something the Ventrue, Lasombra and Giovanni (among others) buy into), and that makes them complicit in the war on the Garou Nation and other Fera. And Vampires are the masters of cities and governments, and therefore Werewolves can easily blame them for pollution and polluting policies.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know all of this, I just had hope that this could be retcon in W20. Because I saw enough hate to werewolves from VtM-fans and I think such scheme just make Garou seems like scum.<br /> <br /> Nope, CoD is way better for me - werewolves at least aren't creeps here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T14:31:03-08:00","id":1052780,"title":"","content":"Because vampires are literally un-natural. They are outside the natural cycle of life and death (and maybe rebirth), things that died and yet still walk around mimicking life, having to feed on the blood of the living to maintain this charade. From the Garou point of view, vampires Should Not Be, and their existence is as much proof of how spiritually broken this world is as that of fomori or the Black Spiral Dancers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T15:06:11-08:00","id":1052809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052686-garou-and-vampires?p=1052696#post1052696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Growing up, pups will be told to not even speak to Vampires, one look and you'll be their slave.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought the majority of werewolves were raised by their human parent(s) and only educated about the Garou religion/philosophy and the existence of the supernatural overall once they start shifting forms upon physical maturity (assuming that werewolves are able to keep tabs on them well enough to find them at that point).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T15:17:12-08:00","id":1052820,"title":"","content":"wondered for a while... can you see any reason for a Garou to object to a Vampire their allied with Dialbrizing Harold Zettler... hes got REALLY potent blood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T15:20:05-08:00","id":1052823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052686-garou-and-vampires?p=1052809#post1052809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I thought the majority of werewolves were raised by their human parent(s) and only educated about the Garou religion/philosophy and the existence of the supernatural overall once they start shifting forms upon physical maturity (assuming that werewolves are able to keep tabs on them well enough to find them at that point).</div> </div> </div> </div>I was under the impression that there were three breeds, Metis, Human-born and Wolf-born, and that the first and last are quite often raised by Garou, while the human-born ones are introduced after the first change (gotta get that alternative sexuality whisking you off on a journey of self-discovery and helping you find your true family metaphor in there after all... Werewolf feels very gay tbh, the werebear crinos form has abs for some reason while the W20 Ananasi look like they were made for Female Gayze and there's a big homoerotic charge, and let's not even get into yiffing...) but to be fair I've read Changing Breeds but not the Core W20 so I'm missing some key knowledge lol.<br /> <br /> Regardless, Vampire 101 is &quot;don't trust them, they'll use their supernatural powers to seem reasonable and friendly when they aren't&quot;, and once that seed is planted no good interactions will happen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T15:22:01-08:00","id":1052825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052686-garou-and-vampires?p=1052820#post1052820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">wondered for a while... can you see any reason for a Garou to object to a Vampire their allied with Dialbrizing Harold Zettler... hes got REALLY potent blood.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;This is a good leech who leeches on other leeches to get more powerful. Every time he does it he reeks even more of the Wyrm. I am okay with this.&quot; - Very, Very Few Garou, If Any.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T15:27:33-08:00","id":1052831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052686-garou-and-vampires?p=1052734#post1052734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know all of this, I just had hope that this could be retcon in W20. Because I saw enough hate to werewolves from VtM-fans and I think such scheme just make Garou seems like scum.<br /> <br /> Nope, CoD is way better for me - werewolves at least aren't creeps here.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course garou are scum!? What the hell......you guys realize this is a game about monsters<br /> <br /> No direct offense to you , but I remember when people played these games with the right tone......<br /> <br /> Who the fuck wants to play all the monsters have a party and get along.....garou can be reasoned with vampires are just trying to make a living etc.....what utter poofiness......","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12902-wisdominchains","name":"WISDOMINCHAINS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12902_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T15:28:37-08:00","id":1052833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052686-garou-and-vampires?p=1052734#post1052734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know all of this, I just had hope that this could be retcon in W20. Because I saw enough hate to werewolves from VtM-fans and I think such scheme just make Garou seems like scum.<br /> <br /> Nope, CoD is way better for me - werewolves at least aren't creeps here.</div> </div> </div> </div>How is not liking vampires being a creep? Even other vampires don't like vampires, and that's something you see intensified even further in the CoD with its predator's taint roll. In Forsaken 2nd, it might boil down to individual choice in prey, but if a pack does pick out a vampire as the target of a hunt, they aren't likely to waver or grant mercy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T15:30:41-08:00","id":1052835,"title":"","content":"For what it's worth it bothers me when werewolf players get all uppity and whine about werewolf being too harsh....these are half animal savages, xenophobic beasts......every time I see stuff about everybody playing nice it makes me sick.........<br /> <br /> Gothic punk ok not folky pop","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12902-wisdominchains","name":"WISDOMINCHAINS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12902_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T15:35:50-08:00","id":1052839,"title":"","content":"I can see a single Garou and a single Vampire having a secret friendship. I could see a pack of garou and a group of vampires having a frenemies type relationship. I can see a sept and a prince of the city have a treaty of non-aggression (Garou have bigger wyrms to kill and Vampires rather not tangle with Lupines.)<br /> <br /> I have this idea for a city of Camarilla that has a treaty with a group of Lupines. They are savage beasts but the Lupines don't break the Masquerade and the Prince doesn't want open war with them. Unfortunately for the Prince, his treaty is with a hive of BSD and the Sabbat have come with a better offer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T15:43:53-08:00","id":1052846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052686-garou-and-vampires?p=1052839#post1052839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can see a single Garou and a single Vampire having a secret friendship. I could see a pack of garou and a group of vampires having a frenemies type relationship. I can see a sept and a prince of the city have a treaty of non-aggression (Garou have bigger wyrms to kill and Vampires rather not tangle with Lupines.)<br /> <br /> I have this idea for a city of Camarilla that has a treaty with a group of Lupines. They are savage beasts but the Lupines don't break the Masquerade and the Prince doesn't want open war with them. Unfortunately for the Prince, his treaty is with a hive of BSD and the Sabbat have come with a better offer.</div> </div> </div> </div>Weren't there old merits for a Vampire to be married to a Werewolf or have one as a close ally?<br /> <br /> My ideal would be a group of Anarch Technothaumaturges who are buddied up with a group of Glass Walkers, maybe some Technosorcerers or a Technopsychic for safe measure. They're total stoners, and they're absolute anarchists. They can't see any point to associate with Vampires or Werewolves beyond those they run into while doing their whole anarch deal.<br /> <br /> The Prince is being a dick? Well now there's a huge facebook event at his haven and everyone's invited, Presence 4 via the invite and his house is SWAMPED... Pentex are building a new refinery out of town? Well now a group of Vampires, Werewolves, Sorcerers and Psychics are planning 12/7 (Vampires need their beauty sleep) to bring it down.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T15:53:16-08:00","id":1052863,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052686-garou-and-vampires?p=1052846#post1052846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Weren't there old merits for a Vampire to be married to a Werewolf or have one as a close ally?</div> </div> </div> </div>To have a companion? Yes. To be <i>married</i>? Kind of... It's called the &quot;I'm in a novel&quot; merit. 0 points, ST fiat only.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T16:01:01-08:00","id":1052869,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052686-garou-and-vampires?p=1052863#post1052863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To have a companion? Yes. To be <i>married</i>? Kind of... It's called the &quot;I'm in a novel&quot; merit. 0 points, ST fiat only.</div> </div> </div> </div>Haha, this was one of those websites which post the merits and half of them are fake. But I am oddly enjoying the idea. A Koldun or Lhiannan and a Garou who fight for a few years, before reconciling their belief systems, something like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T16:15:46-08:00","id":1052881,"title":"","content":"What would be the use of a Garou marrying a Kindred? I mean, talk about giving your Sept a reason to chuck you headfirst into Erebus...<br /> <br /> Anyway, Kindred have a slight advantage when it come to detecting Garou since neonates can have Auspex up to level 5. Imagine a metropolitan area of 1 million people in the USA. There might be four Garou and 20 Kindred. The chances of the local Garou stumbling on the local Kindred is very, very small and the chances that the local Kindred will not notice the Garou before the Garou notices them is even smaller. Smart Kindred will bail and avoid the place where they saw the Garou for a few weeks, just in case. Only terminally incompetent Kindred will be caught randomly by Garou, so it is not a real big loss to Kindred society.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T16:51:44-08:00","id":1052903,"title":"","content":"In the pariahs book it had a doomed romance between a ronin and a caintiff, which ended in her killing him and thinking that it was sadly inevitable.<br /> <br /> A vampire to retain some shred of honor or decensy must control himself and treasure what is left of his humanity<br /> <br /> a Garou must SURRENDER control, rise to the occasion and accept his destiny.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T16:54:19-08:00","id":1052904,"title":"","content":"Other supernaturals don't hate vampires so much. And Garou shouldn't for not being bastards. I mean, yeah, Shadow Lords allowed the alliances with vampires, but even them call them 'eternal foes'. Why them ans werewolves need to be foes. why not just some 'bloodsukers' or something?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T17:06:12-08:00","id":1052914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052686-garou-and-vampires?p=1052904#post1052904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Other supernaturals don't hate vampires so much.</div> </div> </div> </div>Other monsters don't deal with spirits quite so often and subsequently don't see them as bane magnets. Those that can and do see what the Garou see, also hate vampires. Vampires themselves can't really tell the difference between spirits, and so can't really avoid this problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T17:13:40-08:00","id":1052920,"title":"","content":"Amongst the reason it can't work on a global scale (as said, smaller alliances do exist, either individual or group based):<br /> -City/Nature orientation, Vampire wants bigger city has it is their favorite environment &amp; have a higher concentration of prey / Werewolves wants to protect nature for spiritual reason &amp; to protect wolves<br /> -Vampires Prey on humans, that includes kinfolks which are precious to WW<br /> -Vampires when all is said &amp; dones seesother beings as prey/tool/threat, Werewolves are unlikely to be seen as prey, so at some point Kindreds will either try to use them as tool or kill them just in case, and more probably both at the same time, using them in a suicide attack against another threat<br /> -Specific Vampires can also add issues like Tremeres/Kolduns/insert bloodline meddling with Spirits &amp; Caerns, Setites have an history with the Striders &amp; Bubasti, etc etc<br /> -And finally you can add the Wyrm taint<br /> <br /> So I'm rather wondering why they would not be on bad terms?<br /> <br /> Though to be fair most of the time Vampires stay in their city &amp; Weres don't go looking for them<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5462-kendaan","name":"Kendaan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T17:21:46-08:00","id":1052926,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kendaan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052686-garou-and-vampires?p=1052920#post1052920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Amongst the reason it can't work on a global scale (as said, smaller alliances do exist, either individual or group based):<br /> -City/Nature orientation, Vampire wants bigger city has it is their favorite environment &amp; have a higher concentration of prey / Werewolves wants to protect nature for spiritual reason &amp; to protect wolves<br /> -Vampires Prey on humans, that includes kinfolks which are precious to WW<br /> -Vampires when all is said &amp; dones seesother beings as prey/tool/threat, Werewolves are unlikely to be seen as prey, so at some point Kindreds will either try to use them as tool or kill them just in case, and more probably both at the same time, using them in a suicide attack against another threat<br /> -Specific Vampires can also add issues like Tremeres/Kolduns/insert bloodline meddling with Spirits &amp; Caerns, Setites have an history with the Striders &amp; Bubasti, etc etc<br /> -And finally you can add the Wyrm taint<br /> <br /> So I'm rather wondering why they would not be on bad terms?<br /> <br /> Though to be fair most of the time Vampires stay in their city &amp; Weres don't go looking for them</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, al of this is understandable, but Garou still hated by vampire-fans. I heard lot of things - that Garou are hypocrites, fashests and creeps. And I can't deny it, so I agree. IMHO, settle conditions in which werewolves will be enemies of vampires was a wrong move for authors and developers. Its obvious who is more popular, and which faction will get the all hate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T17:30:35-08:00","id":1052932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052686-garou-and-vampires?p=1052926#post1052926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, al of this is understandable, but Garou still hated by vampire-fans. I heard lot of things - that Garou are hypocrites, fashests and creeps. And I can't deny it, so I agree. IMHO, settle conditions in which werewolves will be enemies of vampires was a wrong move for authors and developers. Its obvious who is more popular, and which faction will get the all hate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where do you hear these things? The forum doesn't really feel that way, so I'm guessing it's in your gaming community?<br /> <br /> Honestly I'm unsure what is the problem here, Masquerade &amp; Apocalypse are 2 really different games with different objectives/themes/moods, unless you're trying a crossover and having difficulties to mix WW &amp; Vamps?<br /> <br /> Also, yes, the Werewolves &amp; Fera are monster, but really, Vampires are way worst, it's not even comparable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5462-kendaan","name":"Kendaan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T17:43:25-08:00","id":1052938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, yes, the Werewolves &amp; Fera are monster, but really, Vampires are way worst, it's not even comparable. </div> </div> </div> Only if you care about mortals, whom I don't care about in-setting at all. Even if it will cross the line of &quot;I-spit-on-your-grave&quot; area and will be in 'burn, rape and pillage&quot; way..<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Where do you hear these things? The forum doesn't really feel that way, so I'm guessing it's in your gaming community? </div> </div> </div> Kind of. Discussions about oWoD-metaplot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","user":"Lashet","date":". 02-21-2017, 08:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T18:00:30-08:00","id":1052946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052686-garou-and-vampires?p=1052938#post1052938\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Only if you care about mortals, whom I don't care about in-setting at all. Even if it will cross the line of &quot;I-spit-on-your-grave&quot; area and will be in 'burn, rape and pillage&quot; way..</div> </div> </div> </div>Well not caring about mortal as a base is a good start to be qualified as a monster ha ha And it's also quite consistent with the setting &amp; the path road (unless high humanity)<br /> <br /> And depending on the path/road, sect, clan &amp; age every Vampire is a monster in his own way. And by monster I don't necessarily mean evil. An old Vampire, let's say about a thousand year old (and even way younger than that) doesn't have much human left in him.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052686-garou-and-vampires?p=1052938#post1052938\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kind of. Discussions about oWoD-metaplot.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ouch these tend to get ugly quite fast!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5462-kendaan","name":"Kendaan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T06:23:16-08:00","id":1053157,"title":"","content":"Yes, Garou (and most Fera) will ash low Humanity Kindred (6-) when they find them. It sounds like a fine reason for Kindred to keep to Humanity and to maintain their Humanity. Alternatively, they can learn Auspex, so they can avoid the Garou (or Fera).<br /> <br /> There are a few points where Garou and Kindred can literally profit from a local alliance. The blood of Garou with high levels of Pure Breed is exceptionally powerful and is a valuable commodity in Kindred circles. Garou regeneration allows Garou to produce copious amounts of blood (eight units of blood per day from a Garou in Glabro form would not be unreasonable if the donor received sufficient fluids and nutrition), so a willing donor can provide lots of blood.<br /> <br /> A high Humanity Kindred could potentially make an agreement with a high Pure Breed Garou to supply blood for money. The Garou is paid $100 per unit of blood, allowing the Garou to fight the Wyrm without the worrying about maintaining a job. The Kindred sells the Garou blood for $400 per unit, allowing the Kindred to keep up appearances without worrying about a job. The Garou is capable of focusing on the fight against the Wyrm, the local Camarilla possesses a potent weapon against the Sabbat, and everyone walks away with turning into dust or being stabbed with a silver spoon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T06:59:25-08:00","id":1053169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052686-garou-and-vampires?p=1053157#post1053157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, Garou (and most Fera) will ash low Humanity Kindred (6-) when they find them. It sounds like a fine reason for Kindred to keep to Humanity and to maintain their Humanity. Alternatively, they can learn Auspex, so they can avoid the Garou (or Fera).</div> </div> </div> </div>Caveat: Mokole hate them more than the Garou do, and won't give them any berth at all. Which vampires might try to resist, but certain Gifts make that difficult for them (Tame Subeam, mothersucker!)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There are a few points where Garou and Kindred can literally profit from a local alliance. The blood of Garou with high levels of Pure Breed is exceptionally powerful </div> </div> </div>That was a terrible idea and it never should have made it to print. Much like Vampire's so-called crossover rules, which completely ignore what Traits actually are in other games and how they work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 02-22-2017, 10:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T07:06:34-08:00","id":1053174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052686-garou-and-vampires?p=1053157#post1053157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> There are a few points where Garou and Kindred can literally profit from a local alliance.</div> </div> </div> </div>So while I agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23\" data-vbnamecard=\"23\">Saur Ops Specialist</a> on this, I would not have been so blunt. There are so many holes in this setup and it would fall apart pretty much immediately. This would result in the Garou and/or the Kindred ending up dead. Neither side would tolerate a setup like this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T07:16:28-08:00","id":1053180,"title":"","content":"Whether or not you like the rule, the rule is canon in cWoD and there has been nothing in the 20th edition rules that have negated the previous rule in Revised. While the Garou would probably not tolerate such an alliance if it is discovered (and would likely chuck the offending Garou headfirst into Erebus while ashing any Kindred they can find), I think that the Kindred would turn a blind eye to the entire thing because they would not really want to know the source of the blood. If a neonate is clever enough to acquire Garou blood without upsetting the local Garou, then why ask too many questions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T07:23:03-08:00","id":1053185,"title":"","content":"I think the blood sale could happen. People do that in real life. However, the only people I know who do that are in dire straits. They are unemployed and sell their body fluids because they have nothing else to sell. As soon as their life stabilizes, they stop going to the blood plasma place.<br /> <br /> So a Werewolf in a shitty situation, without other ways to make money, would sell a Vampire their blood. And since this is WoD, this wouldn't be a happy fun transaction. The Vampire would have the power and maybe manipulate the situation where the Werewolf couldn't get stable employment, find kinfolk to support them, etc.<br /> <br /> Also, no Sept wants a vampire to get a hold of Garou blood. While I doubt the Garou know the word &quot;Tremere&quot;, I'm sure they have stories of crazy leech blood magic. Who knows what strange blood magic a Leech could perform on a Garou? I'm sure each cub is warned not to let Leeches to get a hold of your blood.<br /> <br /> So, if a vampire finds a young, stupid werewolf who is desperate enough to defy the wisdom of their elders, then they could get their hands on Werewolf Blood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T07:47:48-08:00","id":1053203,"title":"","content":"In addition to money, Kindred can offer Garou information. Kindred who notice the conflict between the Garou and the local companies could use their powers on the employees of the local companies to gain information that they can sell to the local Garou in exchange for blood (the Kindred can also short the stock in the local companies after they begin to understand that the Garou are going to sabotage the local companies). The young Garou starts rising in the eyes of the elders because he is providing them with valuable intelligence while the Kindred is cashing in on the sabotage that the Garou are committing against the local companies. Eventually, someone is going to find out and be upset, but until then everyone gets what they want.<br /> <br /> Of course, Kindred who are just interested in money and power can forgo the entire blood thing and feed their Garou buddy information for 'free' while betting against the local companies who are their competition. With each act of sabotage, the Garou creates an opportunity for the Kindred to make money and, just as importantly, to grab local talent for their companies when their competitors go out of business. The 'free information' scenario would be much less likely to be discovered by the elders of the Garou (they do no start running into Kindred that smell of Garou blood). When such an information sharing alliance develops, the Kindred who are allied with the Garou become very powerful and very wealthy while the Garou who are allied with the Kindred gains much Renown for leading highly successful missions against local companies who are destroying nature.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T08:19:01-08:00","id":1053222,"title":"","content":"If the Garou grows more powerful, the vampire may start asking for favors in addition to blood. If the Garou disagrees and threatens to ash the vampire, the Vampire could say &quot;If you kill me, my blood mage friend will fuck you up.&quot; Maybe display some horrible leech magic to prove your point. I don't see this going well for the Garou, but awesome for the Vampire.<br /> <br /> High Status Garou makes a bad deal as a Cliath with a Vampire who is now blackmailing them. This sounds like plot for some Garou PCs to root out corruption in their Sept....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":3950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","user":"wonderandawe","date":". 02-22-2017, 11:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T08:37:45-08:00","id":1053231,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">\u200b</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My problem is not that Garou just don't like (or hate) vampires - actually, there are a few factions which like them - but is the described as enemies. </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">You see? </span></span></span><br /> <img src=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/hJgCs-QTS4KTn7kjt0dyOvjIqYrQGEjVJz396fbk_iM_OAwzcNOHi4Y99hioSxiOLL9ISw=s85\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">\u200b</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Why the authors make vampires 'eternal foes'? Sneaky bastards was enough.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","user":"Lashet","date":". 02-22-2017, 11:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T08:40:39-08:00","id":1053237,"title":"","content":"Well, isn't it a common trope, Vampires and Werewolves being long-time enemies? Always thought that was 'a thing' in writing.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","name":"Monalfie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12552_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T08:42:15-08:00","id":1053239,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monalfie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052686-garou-and-vampires?p=1053237#post1053237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, isn't it a common trope, Vampires and Werewolves being long-time enemies? Always thought that was 'a thing' in writing.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think White Wolf may have started the trend. It's one of the reasons why they sued Underworld.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T08:56:22-08:00","id":1053246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Well, isn't it a common trope, Vampires and Werewolves being long-time enemies? </div> </div> </div>Hate it, because werewolves always lose. (remember True Blood)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T11:19:13-08:00","id":1053337,"title":"","content":"No, it was a thing from at least the old horror films, where you had the Wolf Man versus Dracula back in 1943. Garou tend to win against Kindred of the same experience because they are just out-and-out better in combat (elder Kindred have an advantage over Garou because they have centuries of experience and tend to know better than to play fair). An interesting reinterpretation of the conflict can be found at the The Federal Vampire and Zombie Agency (<a href=\"https://www.fvza.org/wandz.html\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.fvza.org/wandz.html</a>), though their werewolves are different than the Garou.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","user":"Aya Tari","date":". 02-22-2017, 02:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T11:29:21-08:00","id":1053339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052686-garou-and-vampires?p=1053180#post1053180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Whether or not you like the rule, the rule is canon in cWoD and there has been nothing in the 20th edition rules that have negated the previous rule in Revised.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Rule&quot; is a strong word for what's written. Can you quote said rule? I'm away from my books, but I'm pretty sure it says something along the lines of: here is a rumor and we aren't going to give a system for it. Oh, and the pure bred Garou are the leader so you need to fight your way through the rank and file to get to them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052686-garou-and-vampires?p=1053180#post1053180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I think that the Kindred would turn a blind eye to the entire thing because they would not really want to know the source of the blood. If a neonate is clever enough to acquire Garou blood without upsetting the local Garou, then why ask too many questions?</div> </div> </div> </div>This screams misunderstanding the Vampire game. No Elder would ever let a neonate have a source of power and &quot;not ask too many questions&quot;. That just isn't a thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052686-garou-and-vampires?p=1053185#post1053185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> So a Werewolf in a shitty situation, without other ways to make money, would sell a Vampire their blood.</div> </div> </div> </div>They wouldn't. The ones that might end up in the situation you are describing don't have Pure Breed. And Werewolves don't generally <i>need</i> money. And have easier ways of getting it anyways. There is a level 2 (?) fetish that is literally unlimited money from ATMs.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052686-garou-and-vampires?p=1053185#post1053185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> So, if a vampire finds a young, stupid werewolf who is desperate enough to defy the wisdom of their elders, then they could get their hands on Werewolf Blood.</div> </div> </div> </div>This could be an interesting story. But it would be a fairly unique one because of the circumstances having to line up just right to let it happen. <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052686-garou-and-vampires?p=1053246#post1053246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hate it, because werewolves always lose. (remember True Blood)</div> </div> </div> </div>True Blood has terribly weak werewolves. They in no way represent Garou. Besides, the show is all about Vampires. I think similar happens in Twilight (haven't read it for myself).<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T11:35:05-08:00","id":1053347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052686-garou-and-vampires?p=1053157#post1053157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A high Humanity Kindred could potentially make an agreement with a high Pure Breed Garou to supply blood for money. The Garou is paid $100 per unit of blood, allowing the Garou to fight the Wyrm without the worrying about maintaining a job. The Kindred sells the Garou blood for $400 per unit, allowing the Kindred to keep up appearances without worrying about a job. The Garou is capable of focusing on the fight against the Wyrm, the local Camarilla possesses a potent weapon against the Sabbat, and everyone walks away with turning into dust or being stabbed with a silver spoon.</div> </div> </div> </div> I feel like even the idea of Vampires buying blood from one another, especially in the context that they can, you know, magically bind someone to their will if their blood is being drank is... Questionable.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","name":"Monalfie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12552_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T11:42:26-08:00","id":1053351,"title":"","content":"The specific rule is from Vampire Storytellers Handbook: Revised (p. 137). Garou are capable of recovering one blood point per hour and, if the Garou possesses Pure Breed, Kindred gain the following benefits when they spend a minimum of one blood point of Garou blood per turn:<br /> <br /> 1: 1 additional action.<br /> 2: 1 additional action and 1 automatic success on Strength rolls.<br /> 3: 2 additional actions and 1 automatic success on Strength rolls.<br /> 4: 2 additional actions and 2 automatic successes on Strength rolls.<br /> 5: 3 additional actions and 3 automatic successes on Strength rolls.<br /> <br /> Of course, every point of Garou blood in the system of a Kindred increases the difficulty to resist frenzy by one, so it should probably be drank only before a major conflict, when frenzy is acceptable. However, most Kindred can deal with a +1 difficulty to frenzy rolls, so it would not be unreasonable for someone worried about a conflict to drink one point of Garou blood beforehand, assuming they have access to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T12:23:58-08:00","id":1053366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052686-garou-and-vampires?p=1053351#post1053351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The specific rule is from Vampire Storytellers Handbook: Revised (p. 137). Garou are capable of recovering one blood point per hour and, if the Garou possesses Pure Breed, Kindred gain the following benefits when they spend a minimum of one blood point of Garou blood per turn:<br /> <br /> 1: 1 additional action.<br /> 2: 1 additional action and 1 automatic success on Strength rolls.<br /> 3: 2 additional actions and 1 automatic success on Strength rolls.<br /> 4: 2 additional actions and 2 automatic successes on Strength rolls.<br /> 5: 3 additional actions and 3 automatic successes on Strength rolls.<br /> <br /> Of course, every point of Garou blood in the system of a Kindred increases the difficulty to resist frenzy by one, so it should probably be drank only before a major conflict, when frenzy is acceptable. However, most Kindred can deal with a +1 difficulty to frenzy rolls, so it would not be unreasonable for someone worried about a conflict to drink one point of Garou blood beforehand, assuming they have access to it.</div> </div> </div> </div>And Mummy blood increases your Humanity. These rules were always dumb. Just say that Werewolf blood tastes amazing and drinking it restores extra blood and Willpower. Don't make it into a power-up resource. Same for Mummies and other oddities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T13:19:37-08:00","id":1053391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052686-garou-and-vampires?p=1053351#post1053351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The specific rule is from Vampire Storytellers Handbook: Revised (p. 137). Garou are capable of recovering one blood point per hour and, if the Garou possesses Pure Breed, Kindred gain the following benefits when they spend a minimum of one blood point of Garou blood per turn:<br /> <br /> 1: 1 additional action.<br /> 2: 1 additional action and 1 automatic success on Strength rolls.<br /> 3: 2 additional actions and 1 automatic success on Strength rolls.<br /> 4: 2 additional actions and 2 automatic successes on Strength rolls.<br /> 5: 3 additional actions and 3 automatic successes on Strength rolls.<br /> <br /> Of course, every point of Garou blood in the system of a Kindred increases the difficulty to resist frenzy by one, so it should probably be drank only before a major conflict, when frenzy is acceptable. However, most Kindred can deal with a +1 difficulty to frenzy rolls, so it would not be unreasonable for someone worried about a conflict to drink one point of Garou blood beforehand, assuming they have access to it.</div> </div> </div> </div>So that's the first time I've seen the rule written out (thanks). Every other iteration of the game doesn't bother and just implies some bonus Discipline levels. This version makes as little or less sense.<br /> And its directly contradicted by the Werewolf core books (all of them). Garou certainly recover blood faster than 1 per hour since blood loss (in system) in represented by bashing/lethal damage levels. And Regeneration replenishes those.<br /> This is also the only time I can think of that there is the implication that Vampires can choose which blood points in their system to spend. So that's an added level of rules confusion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T18:21:26-08:00","id":1053556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052686-garou-and-vampires?p=1053239#post1053239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I think White Wolf may have started the trend. It's one of the reasons why they sued Underworld.</div> </div> </div> </div>They'd honestly have had a better case if they'd tried suing the people who made the first Blade movie, IMO.<br /> <br /> As for the vampires vs werewolves trope, it goes back as far as an episode of &quot;The Real Ghostbusters&quot; back in the 1980s, and before that there are odds and ends such as the Spanish horror films Los Monstrous del Terror/Dracula vs Frankenstein (1970) and La Noche de Walpurgis/Werewolf Shadow/Werewolf vs The Vampire Woman (1971). I suspect it's just a natural result of things to want to see two famous monsters fight. The same way Godzilla vs King Kong or Freddy vs Jason came about. <br /> <br /> In the World of Darkness, it always struck me as the natural outgrowth of both societies. The Kindred are a perfect storm of arrogance and paranoia that only a bunch of immortals who still run the risk of violent death can be, while the Garou are a dying breed of religious crusaders with the pure zealotry that can only come with having objective proof that your beliefs are true, and both are apex predators who instinctively want to be in charge of whatever territory they're standing on at the moment. <br /> (This doesn't even get into something like the Silent Striders, who have a historical reason for hating the undead on top of all that.)<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T02:20:04-08:00","id":1053719,"title":"","content":"There was also Frankenstein meets the Wolfman, as well as a Laural &amp; Hardy version.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5818-eviltyger","name":"EvilTyger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T06:53:50-08:00","id":1053795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052686-garou-and-vampires?p=1053556#post1053556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They'd honestly have had a better case if they'd tried suing the people who made the first Blade movie, IMO.</div> </div> </div> </div>Blade predates WW by 18 years.<br /> <br /> Did you read the <i>Underworld</i> filing? <i>Underworld</i> had over 100 listed similarities to a novel published by WW. Some of them were preposterous, but some were actually kind of suspicious. The sort of thing where WW sues Sony just in case and Sony gives WW fans a bunch of free passes to the film to mollify them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T08:30:45-08:00","id":1053832,"title":"","content":"Though, as a WtA fan, I thought that Underworld was just prejudiced against Garou. This is the WtA forum, so 'Lupine' is just a racial slur thrown around by Kindred who lack a proper appreciation of Garou culture, usually right before an irritated Garou rips their heads off and stuffs their heads another Kindred's rear end. I do wonder what a proper treatment of the Garou would look like in the movies (I imagine that the special effects budget would be quite large).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T12:51:49-08:00","id":1053961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>etherial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052686-garou-and-vampires?p=1053795#post1053795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Blade predates WW by 18 years.<br /> <br /> Did you read the <i>Underworld</i> filing? <i>Underworld</i> had over 100 listed similarities to a novel published by WW. Some of them were preposterous, but some were actually kind of suspicious. The sort of thing where WW sues Sony just in case and Sony gives WW fans a bunch of free passes to the film to mollify them.</div> </div> </div> </div>The character of Blade predates WW, not the film. Blade as introduced in Marvel's Tomb of Dracula (of which I've read the entire run) originated on the idea of &quot;what if Shaft was a vampire hunter&quot; and grew from there. The film on the other hand, borrowed a bit from Vampire, especially in it's inclusion of vampire &quot;houses/tribes&quot;, one of which was pretty much the Assamites with an ethnicity swap. <br /> <br /> And yes, I read the entirety of the filing back when it was first made. I've also discussed it with several people who made depositions for the case, and have heard accounts of the company's rather weird involvement with Hollywood starting with the Kindred the Embraced show and why this probably doomed the suit from the beginning. While they may have had a better case against the makers of Blade, odds are that any copyright lawsuit against any film maker would've failed. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-06T11:57:17-07:00","id":1088811,"title":"","content":"Hi!<br /> <br /> This &quot;Vampire and Werewolves are eternal enemies&quot; comes mostly from WW and incredibly bad horror movies, but what I find even more annoying was WW making the the Werewolves super-warriors in WtA! Because this runs counter to almost all old lore. While the werewolves were devastating agianst anything mortal, against other supernaturals they were not that good. There is nothing wrong to add to the lore, but WtA pushed the envelope on counter to anything.<br /> Vampires and Werewolves rarely popped up in the same stories and if, then the Lupines were either among the Vampire forces &quot;foot soldiers&quot; or when they went against each other, Night\u00b4s Dark Masters won most of the time. Only very seldom the Werewolves won and then normally only with a lot of outside help.<br /> <br /> Among the authors of WtA seems to be a number of moon-addicts and guys with a serious hard-on for the Werewolf girls, because anybody knowing a bit about the legends can only shake the head about the OP hack\u00b4n slay concoction WtA is. The cranked up Damage soaking is way beyond anything shown in the legends, a ton of the gifts and rites are far more out than a number of weird stuff VtM got. In the Vampire legends, strange powers are not unusual, but Werewolf legends have fewer strange powers, esp on the spiritual side! Werewolves are much more IQ- addling bloodlust on legs than the Vampires are, even in the old legends.<br /> Adding to the problem is a subset of WtA players who even go more out there when interpreting rules. WtA is already OP by any kind of legend, but their claims what the Werwolves are supposedly capable of is not even written in these rules, neither intended. That is one reason why many Vampire players, esp those knowing old legends, are not too keen on WtA.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7492,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7492-g\u00fcnther","user":"G\u00fcnther","date":". 05-06-2017, 03:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7492-g\u00fcnther","name":"G\u00fcnther","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-06T12:11:02-07:00","id":1088817,"title":"","content":"How so? In many cultures, werewolves were evil sorcerers, mystical shamans, savage warriors, or just another type of vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-06T17:27:26-07:00","id":1088916,"title":"","content":"I see no issue with soaking agg...the resiliance is not too unfounded in werewolf lore. Some of the legends put a big emphasis on the need for <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=GhxcL2-wo3M\" target=\"_blank\">silver</a> or fire. Honestly the weakest werewolves I've seen came from more recent versions (i.e. True Blood)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","user":"CeltSPZ","date":". 05-07-2017, 01:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-06T18:16:21-07:00","id":1088930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>G\u00fcnther</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052686-garou-and-vampires?p=1088811#post1088811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi!<br /> <br /> This &quot;Vampire and Werewolves are eternal enemies&quot; comes mostly from WW and incredibly bad horror movies, but what I find even more annoying was WW making the the Werewolves super-warriors in WtA! Because this runs counter to almost all old lore. .</div> </div> </div> </div>And yet you have no problem with Vampires as something other than unintelligent zombies who were burried wrong...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-06T19:12:08-07:00","id":1088950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>G\u00fcnther</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052686-garou-and-vampires?p=1088811#post1088811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Among the authors of WtA seems to be a number of moon-addicts and guys with a serious hard-on for the Werewolf girls,</div> </div> </div> </div>I knew close to a dozen Werewolf writers back during the revised period, and find this rather insulting and offensive. I would consider flagging it if I didn't believe such a thing should be reserved for more serious offenses than this sort of trite foolishness. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-06T19:40:01-07:00","id":1088961,"title":"","content":"Could a Garou and a Kindred have a romantic relationship? Sure: 'forbidden love' is a major plot device used just about everywhere.<br /> <br /> Will it end well...? No it will most assuredly <i>not</i>. But then, 'tragic love' is <i>also</i> a cherished plot device.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-06T19:55:49-07:00","id":1088968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052686-garou-and-vampires?p=1088930#post1088930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And yet you have no problem with Vampires as something other than unintelligent zombies who were burried wrong...</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd just be happy to see some of these cited &quot;legends&quot; be given names. Are we talking about Herodotus and the Neuri? Lycaon? Ovid's Metamorphosis? Turkic Kurtadam? Bisclavret? The Ulfhednar? Prince Vseslav of Belarus? Vlkolaks? Henry Boguet's work as a demonologist? The She Wolves of Julich? The Beast of Gevaudan? Livonian Hounds of God? Navajo skin-walkers? The Wendigo? Hatian je-rouge? P'an Hu? Red Riding Hood? Guhin? Warren Zevon? Alan Moore? What?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-06T19:59:12-07:00","id":1088969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052686-garou-and-vampires?p=1088961#post1088961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could a Garou and a Kindred have a romantic relationship? Sure: 'forbidden love' is a major plot device used just about everywhere.<br /> <br /> Will it end well...? No it will most assuredly <i>not</i>. But then, 'tragic love' is <i>also</i> a cherished plot device.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd actually put in the top five reasons to do a crossover game. <br /> <br /> Also, &quot;Pentex is moving in on our Sire's business holdings&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-06T20:13:34-07:00","id":1088973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052686-garou-and-vampires?p=1088968#post1088968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd just be happy to see some of these cited &quot;legends&quot; be given names. Are we talking about Herodotus and the Neuri? Lycaon? Ovid's Metamorphosis? Turkic Kurtadam? Bisclavret? The Ulfhednar? Prince Vseslav of Belarus? Vlkolaks? Henry Boguet's work as a demonologist? The She Wolves of Julich? The Beast of Gevaudan? Livonian Hounds of God? Navajo skin-walkers? The Wendigo? Hatian je-rouge? P'an Hu? Red Riding Hood? Guhin? Warren Zevon? Alan Moore? What?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Also a good point I just found the juxtiposition of the werewolves aren't enough like myths with &quot;Vampires are super awesome lords of the Night&quot; as hiliarious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-06T21:05:19-07:00","id":1088993,"title":"","content":"Its rather obvious. Garou are Old Testament, like old school primordial Caveman Old Testament. They are hypocritical, and savage, but ultimately they are divine monsters for a reason, because if they were gone and none of the shapeshifters took their place the World ends because they are the Antibodies of the Universe. Caerns are Soul Organs of the World, when compromised the World literally lessens.<br /> <br /> Vampires meanwhile exist for themselves. If ultimately they were no more, the world would in all likelyhood improve a great deal. They are the biggest criminal organization in the Universe, and stheir undead, and literally cursed, existence favors a downward spiral. While good Cainites can exist, their whole species favors rather unwholesome practices as the path of least resistance, hence the Salubri are nearly Extinct. The Children of Osiris don't sire for a reason, because Osiris realizes his state of Vampirism was an abominaiton to Ma'at, so instead he developed a Cult to teach others, the whole philosophy of its better to adopt then birth new children when their are too many children already, and in Osiris' case one vampire is too many. The Ahrimanes even hint at this, their Weakness of Sterility, hints at being an Animistic taboo, which allows them to learn Spiritus, as they become less of a parasitic Virus and a more of a contained benign tumor.<br /> <br /> Garou also lump all Vampires together so Laibon, Cainites, Wan Kuei, and anything else that drinks blood, is dead and hates sunlight. And their overwhelming 10k+ history of interaction with the point towards a hostile relationship, one of the 16 Tribes even lost their Physical Homeland, and Spiritual Homeland, and connection to their ancestors because of one of the Vampire's. The Wan Xian tricked not just the Garou but all the Beast Courts, and even other divine shen, such as the Hsien.<br /> <br /> So even if you really were a good nice guy vampire, its generally accepted the polite merciful thing to do would be to euthanize you. But if you go with real Politik then I would say if you are a Vampire and really want to get along, say maybe you were Kin, then do something along the lines of making a Spirit Sanctified Oath Not to sire progeny, maybe even spiritually neuter yourself, and promise to try to not contribute to Anti-Gaian wyrmish deeds. This is why in 1st gen you even had things like a Golconda Child of Osiris being known to a Stargazer Sept and accepted. If you have a place under Heaven/the Cycle then you are less like the rest of the Vampires. Thus Revised Era Path of Paradox, Blood, Humanity and Harmony/Feral Heart would be likely the most compatible with the Garou as they are really the only ones that would give themselves a place that jives with the Cycle of the World.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-06T23:09:11-07:00","id":1089015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>G\u00fcnther</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052686-garou-and-vampires?p=1088811#post1088811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Among the authors of WtA seems to be a number of moon-addicts and guys with a serious hard-on for the Werewolf girls, because anybody knowing a bit about the legends can only shake the head about the OP hack\u00b4n slay concoction WtA is.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Nope, that kind of insult slinging is not OK. Take some time off.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T05:42:13-07:00","id":1089084,"title":"","content":"Wyrm taint is pretty much all the reason the Garou need. Vampires attract banes and bane activity, are quite possibly (according to garou cosmology) some ancient type of self sustaining self replicating Formori and yeah... Banes. Where you find Vampires there will be Banes, the exact kind of environment that is good for vampiric hunting is the exact same kind of environment that lends strength to the Weaver and the Wyrm (especially the Wyrm). Vampires are a walking corruption of the Natural Cycle and Gaia's laws. Did I mention the Banes? <br /> <br /> Kindred/Cainites and Garou are monsters in different ways, the horror flavour of the game lines express in different ways. Vampires and Werewolves fighting has always been a thing, the why depends on the Game Line. In VTM the Lupines are savage and deadly monsters that the Vampires tend to know very little about and have no real idea on why they are so hostile to Vampires only that they are, possibly something to do with the Curse of Caine (yes CURSE), exceptions to the rule exist but typically the Lupines are deadly beasts and little more (much in flavour with the Lycans in Underworld etc). From the WTA point of view, well see what I already wrote.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T09:21:24-07:00","id":1089203,"title":"","content":"Asked once does a Lhiannan need 5 dots of Ogham, for a Garou to move past &quot;Leech! Kill it!&quot; to form a grudging truce with a gangrel just to rid gaia of this <i>thing</i>!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T09:32:51-07:00","id":1089208,"title":"","content":"All Kindred need to do is maintain a Humanity 7+ and be subtle about their feeding (animal blood six days a week and human blood on the seventh would be subtle enough) to avoid attention from the Garou. If the Garou cannot sense the Wyrm taint on you and do not overhear any reports of blood-drinking fiends, they have better things to do than hunting down hypothetical Kindred.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T09:52:33-07:00","id":1089222,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052686-garou-and-vampires?p=1089208#post1089208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All Kindred need to do is maintain a Humanity 7+ and be subtle about their feeding (animal blood six days a week and human blood on the seventh would be subtle enough) to avoid attention from the Garou. If the Garou cannot sense the Wyrm taint on you and do not overhear any reports of blood-drinking fiends, they have better things to do than hunting down hypothetical Kindred.</div> </div> </div> </div>....until you reach sufficient age animal vitae can no longer provide nourishment. <i>And</i> you never frenzy around others. <i>And</i> obsessively maintain the Masquerade.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T09:55:46-07:00","id":1089226,"title":"","content":"When does age have anything to do about making animal vitae unable to provide nourishment? This is cWoD not nWoD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T10:40:33-07:00","id":1089253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052686-garou-and-vampires?p=1089226#post1089226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When does age have anything to do about making animal vitae unable to provide nourishment? This is cWoD not nWoD.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, it's the same, in this regard. The older a vampire, the more and more potent vitae must be to subsist off of. The Chronicles of Darkness give hard numbers for this stuff; the World of Darkness doesn't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T11:27:00-07:00","id":1089273,"title":"","content":"Not really. If there is no mechanism for it to occur in cWoD, it is just fluff unsupported by the rules. The Elder Thirst has specific mechanisms for excluding animal and human blood, but there is no corollary for excluding just animal blood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T11:36:59-07:00","id":1089279,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052686-garou-and-vampires?p=1089203#post1089203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Asked once does a Lhiannan need 5 dots of Ogham, for a Garou to move past &quot;Leech! Kill it!&quot; to form a grudging truce with a gangrel just to rid gaia of this <i>thing</i>!</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, yes, the Lhiannan. I wish I could remember who it was on the usenet boards who said it was no wonder they went extinct, given that their special discipline was the ability to piss off every other supernatural being in the game. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> You could probably do a decent Dark Ages (or pre-Dark Ages) one shot around that idea. This one vampire witch is mucking up all the local flow of spiritual energy, causing causing a small group of vampires and a small werewolf pack to have to join forces to put and end to it. Hmm, maybe a woad-painted Gangrel barbarian warrior, a hot-blooded red-haired Brujah clan princess, and a weird Salubri bard, with a pair of Fianna and a Silver Fang of House Austere Howl. You could also toss in a nosy Corax along for the ride, a mage of the Old Faith or Spirit Talker stripe (or even a Hermetic of House Diedne or Merinita), and a changeling sent by one of the Courts as an observer. Would probably make for a good convention game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T15:00:26-07:00","id":1089407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052686-garou-and-vampires?p=1089279#post1089279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ah, yes, the Lhiannan. I wish I could remember who it was on the usenet boards who said it was no wonder they went extinct, given that their special discipline was the ability to piss off every other supernatural being in the game. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> You could probably do a decent Dark Ages (or pre-Dark Ages) one shot around that idea. This one vampire witch is mucking up all the local flow of spiritual energy, causing causing a small group of vampires and a small werewolf pack to have to join forces to put and end to it. Hmm, maybe a woad-painted Gangrel barbarian warrior, a hot-blooded red-haired Brujah clan princess, and a weird Salubri bard, with a pair of Fianna and a Silver Fang of House Austere Howl. You could also toss in a nosy Corax along for the ride, a mage of the Old Faith or Spirit Talker stripe (or even a Hermetic of House Diedne or Merinita), and a changeling sent by one of the Courts as an observer. Would probably make for a good convention game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, once they're done with the Lhiannan, the Corax can use the 79 Degrees and Sunny Grenade (aka rite of the sun's bright ray) to tie up those pesky vampiric loose ends. Then the fae and the changers jump the mages, who are arguing about who is right, and agree to part ways, having killed three birds with one stone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T16:01:51-07:00","id":1089439,"title":"","content":"Thing a Lhinian with less then 5 dots of Ogham can offend the Garou enough to forge truces with other leeches? was what I was thinking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T23:22:54-07:00","id":1089603,"title":"","content":"Obviously, you can have exceptional alliances or even friendships between vampires and werewolves. I don't think that you can have it on a later scale though, not without making major changes to Werewolf. I don't even think that you could change Vampire enough that werewolves could like them. The kind of creature that vampires (undead and immortal) are is going to be antithetical to nature and so at odds with werewolves. <br /> <br /> Of course, lots of people like crossovers and there are all sorts of justifications that you can come up with to explain why some werewolves and vampires are allying. I've noticed that role players love to break rules - good Drow, Son of Cacophony, Abomination, etc. Vampire and werewolf friendships are just one thing on that list. Tell people that they can't do something and they want to do it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T05:54:09-07:00","id":1089730,"title":"","content":"why are good Drow so much more common then good Gnoll's or Bugbears?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T06:00:56-07:00","id":1089734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052686-garou-and-vampires?p=1089730#post1089730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">why are good Drow so much more common then good Gnoll's or Bugbears?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because people want to play a drow rather then a gnoll or a bugbear.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T06:07:39-07:00","id":1089737,"title":"","content":"is it just the innate magic, or they look sexier?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T06:10:38-07:00","id":1089739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052686-garou-and-vampires?p=1089737#post1089737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">is it just the innate magic, or they look sexier?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes..........","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T06:19:23-07:00","id":1089742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052686-garou-and-vampires?p=1089737#post1089737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">is it just the innate magic, or they look sexier?</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, depending on edition there were other complications.<br /> <br /> Plus Drizzt.<br /> <br /> On topic though, crossovers are easier to maintain if the ST and players are willing to accept that their game's WOD is 