<div class=\"message\">Shouldn't that actually be all the more reason for a tribe of all women to allow trans women? If breeding is so important, having women in the group that can impregnate other women in the group sounds like win-win.</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't shake out quite so evenly there, given the first tenet of the Litany and all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-09T09:51:41-07:00","id":1090340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052686-garou-and-vampires?p=1090326#post1090326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It doesn't shake out quite so evenly there, given the first tenet of the Litany and all.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see. It seems my lack of WtA knowledge is showing.<br /> <br /> EDIT: oh, wait, that's the &quot;werewolves can't mate with other werewolves&quot; thing. Duh.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-09T11:34:24-07:00","id":1090390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052686-garou-and-vampires?p=1090123#post1090123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It depends on the edition. Sometimes males are allowed and completed tolerated even if they are less common than females. In one revised edition book they said that all male DoC's had been purged and you're a bad person (as a player) if you want to play one.</div> </div> </div> </div>IIRC, it was all of them had been purged save one transgendered member. I think Justin Achilli had explained on usenet why he decided to do this, but at least part of it was that it was supposed to be another sign of the End Times prompted by whatever it is that causes the music members of the bloodline hear in their heads. <br /> <br /> I eventually decided that, in my game, their blood just has a negative reaction to Y chromosomes that leads to a failed embrace (using the rules for Abominations as a guideline, a success gives you a Caitiff, a failure a dead body, and a botch something that's closer to full-dead than undead). But this is part of my tweaking of the bloodline into a bunch of modern Dionysian maenads who only appeared in the past 100 years or so as a sign of the coming End Times. YMMV.<br /> <br /> Oddly, I never heard of anyone wanting to play a male Ahrimane. I wonder why. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-09T11:38:07-07:00","id":1090393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052686-garou-and-vampires?p=1090222#post1090222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean I'm not the most thrilled about Evan Heals the Past being a white blond kid with white parents specifically chosen by Wendigo because ages ago he had a drop of Native blood... Really Wendigo doesn't seem like the most progressive of Spirits...</div> </div> </div> </div>I recall Ethan Skemp saying this was why John North-Wind's Son replaced Evan as the tribe's signature character in the revised edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-09T12:23:42-07:00","id":1090427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EvilTyger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052686-garou-and-vampires?p=1090183#post1090183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not displeased so much with the action, but the (in game) reasoning behind it. The totem has changed to reflected a changed world. This should be explored.</div> </div> </div> </div>Though this might be said to beg the question, &quot;why would an ancient spirit that predates the very concept of human civilization feel it needs to change to reflect the beliefs of a bunch of primates?&quot; Even more so given that it certainly didn't change to reflect human views on gender during the middle ages, the Renaissance or the Victorian period.<br /> <br /> I'm reminded of the Sandman arc &quot;A Game of You&quot;, in which the ancient witch Thessaly tells the transgendered Wanda that the ritual she's working won't work for Wanda, because Hecate won't allow it. Ancient forces may not necessarily conform with modern social beliefs. (And as an aside, while Gaiman's story might nowadays be decried as being trans-odious*, at the time is was pretty progressive and risky for just including a transgendered character at all. I'm sure that 30 years from now, a new generation of gamers will be angrily decrying how backwards and hateful we all are for something completely under 99% of society's social radar.) But, I don't necessarily care how people handle the issue in their own games. I, personally, tweaked the Lions of Zion in Mage to allow female members, even if the group does still respect traditional Jewish gender issues regarding Kabbalah. But I don't allow female Sons of Mitra or male Sisters of Gabrielle in the Celestial Chorus. So, I've no idea if I'm being sexist or cis-something, or what. <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\">*<sub>I refuse to use the term &quot;phobic&quot; anymore, because dislike or hatred is not the same thing as fear. I dislike teenagers; I am not afraid of them. However, I am afraid of bees. </sub></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-09T13:25:18-07:00","id":1090455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052686-garou-and-vampires?p=1090427#post1090427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Though this might be said to beg the question, &quot;why would an ancient spirit that predates the very concept of human civilization feel it needs to change to reflect the beliefs of a bunch of primates?&quot; Even more so given that it certainly didn't change to reflect human views on gender during the middle ages, the Renaissance or the Victorian period.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because it's an ancient spirit that was, apparently, maimed and/or wrong by one of said primates, and they're kind of on said spirit's shit list now, at least as far as asshole machismo goes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-09T14:19:49-07:00","id":1090478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052686-garou-and-vampires?p=1090455#post1090455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Because it's an ancient spirit that was, apparently, maimed and/or wrong by one of said primates, and they're kind of on said spirit's shit list now, at least as far as asshole machismo goes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I fully grok the idea that Pegasus is a gynocentric entity. I just think there is a valid question as to why current human positions on transgenderism should matter to Pegasus any more or any less than, for example, 18th century positions on how or in what subjects women should be educated or the medieval Catholic Church's position on the role woman have in the concept of Original Sin. (My personal take on the issue of Pegasus and accepting male-to-female transgender Garou as possible Black Furies is &quot;maybe&quot;, as a case by case basis likely requiring one to go above and beyond to prove her worth and Pegasus likely having some sort of obtuse agenda that doesn't make sense to mere mortals. Because gods are weird that way.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-09T16:07:52-07:00","id":1090511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052686-garou-and-vampires?p=1090478#post1090478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I fully grok the idea that Pegasus is a gynocentric entity. I just think there is a valid question as to why current human positions on transgenderism should matter to Pegasus any more or any less than, for example, 18th century positions on how or in what subjects women should be educated or the medieval Catholic Church's position on the role woman have in the concept of Original Sin. (My personal take on the issue of Pegasus and accepting male-to-female transgender Garou as possible Black Furies is &quot;maybe&quot;, as a case by case basis likely requiring one to go above and beyond to prove her worth and Pegasus likely having some sort of obtuse agenda that doesn't make sense to mere mortals. Because gods are weird that way.)</div> </div> </div> </div>In the 18th century, those rules maintained the status quo of 'women are less than men'. Now, women are running countries, marital rape has been outlawed on most of two continents, and gender has become less binary in many eyes.<br /> <br /> Other than a few pockets of folklore, there has never really been as radical a shift, or as measurable, as what has occured since WWII.<br /> <br /> Case in point for potential 'Male Black Fury', Elliot Stabler from Law &amp; Order: SVU. Overreactivelly protective of his own family, voilently reactive to percieved injustices, constantly challenging his own religion's view on binary sexuality, and could easily be compared to a mother wolf for any harmed child he runs across.<br /> <br /> The questions at this point are &quot;What does the game gain by maintainig the status quo?&quot; vs &quot;What does the game gain by shaking it up?&quot;. I see a lot more potential in the later.<br /> <br /> BUT, whomever handles the situation needs to put the effort in to addressing it. Changing things by hand wave might work for giving Malkavians Dementation, This change, not so much.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5818-eviltyger","name":"EvilTyger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-09T16:49:52-07:00","id":1090520,"title":"","content":"I favor the Black Furies not accepting of transwomen. Which is not a judgement regarding transgender people, but rather about the Black Furies. A person of obviously African descent isn't going to be able to show up to a KKK meeting and ask for membership because he says he has the mind of a white person. Likewise, someone with a male body is unlikely to find acceptance in the Black Furies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-09T17:17:17-07:00","id":1090527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052686-garou-and-vampires?p=1090520#post1090520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I favor the Black Furies not accepting of transwomen. Which is not a judgement regarding transgender people, but rather about the Black Furies. A person of obviously African descent isn't going to be able to show up to a KKK meeting and ask for membership because he says he has the mind of a white person. Likewise, someone with a male body is unlikely to find acceptance in the Black Furies.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a very deeply flawed statement on so many levels. Let's peel them away and examine them.<br /> <br /> The Furies, you see, are often subject to changes and shakeups. They're the proclaimed guardians of the Wyld in this age, after all; They couldn't be that averse to changing their tunes as a tribe. Change is something that they venerate.<br /> <br /> As to their comparison with a hate group espousing superiority of an already privileged group, wow. The vigilantism of the Black Furies is something that props up the helpless. The KKK is one of the forces standing against said helpless groups. I'd say you had it backward, but that would imply that the Furies were all about stacking up piles of male genitals as metrics for success, when their membership usually takes the subtler, quieter, and less traditionally accepted tacks of combating the Wyrm. And see how much flak they get for it.<br /> <br /> Related to that point, though it's really more of a footnote or rider type of correction, the opposite point of view is not logical. Hate gets that way, and such KKK members might accept such an individual. Self-hating members of minorities would be &quot;the good ones&quot; to them, to demonstrate the odious nature of that concept.<br /> <br /> As to the subject of trans identity, the Furies would probably entertain that. They lived among horse-riding nomads before they descended on Greece, and as such, wouldn't have had the same ideas that settled folk had about gender identity, or would have clung to them on account of ideas they had and shared before finding a group of kin with them. Therefore, it's not unreasonable to assume that the Furies might have been accepting transgender women all the time, but were written the way they were due to the blind spots of past contributors right up to the concept of the game coming about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-10T06:16:46-07:00","id":1090701,"title":"","content":"I hardly think that being against child molesters, rapists, slavers, and wife beaters makes someone part of a hate group. I would think that if someone is not against those things, they probably have more in common with the members of hate groups than they should be comfortable with. Yes, Black Furies focus on fighting the Wyrm by protecting the innocent and punishing the wicked. In most societies, the vast majority of the wicked are men (which is not saying that most men are wicked people, just that most of the wicked people are men). Whether that is some innate weakness of men or just a matter of greater opportunities for wickedness for men is unknown.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[