class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052686-garou-and-vampires?p=1090971#post1090971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just because a spirit does not actively disapprove does not mean that the Garou approve. We do not talk about Get of Fenris being murdering, raping bastards because their totem once tolerated Vikings</div> </div> </div> </div>Hasn't Fenris always advocated tearing vikings apart and leaving their bodies to rot as a warning to Wotan?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T08:11:47-07:00","id":1091135,"title":"","content":"\u200bOf course the morality system of WoD is wonky, giving modern anthropomorphic perspective to everything.<br /> <br /> Vampires are cannibal corpses, clearly cursed by spirits. Why should werewolves that have exterminated other shapeshifters and even other Garou tribes feel any sort of sympathy towards them? Why should anyone? What good are they?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-12T16:41:16-07:00","id":1091755,"title":"","content":"At best, they serve as a control on humans, but they have not been doing that very well since the 14th century.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-12T16:58:06-07:00","id":1091764,"title":"","content":"<b>CT Phipps' take on it</b><br /> <br /> I have the view that werewolves have a variety of reasons why they hate vampires. However, the real reason isn't because they're unnatural or even Wyrm tainted (what isn't, lately?). No, the real reason werewolves hate vampires is they hate the majority of other GAROU. Vampires are also controlling evil bastards (like powerful humans). They're competition for the world and powerful predators so OF COURSE they loathe each other.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T03:26:07-07:00","id":1092294,"title":"","content":"Hmm In my opinion every tribe have something against leeches in some ways so Garou nation has. The best sample - Shadow Lords. Vampires infested their homeland and lords had to defend themselves, maby their kinfolk. Tzimisce are tough fiends so I guess the war never ended. For example tribes that defend Wyld, creator, life (Red Talons, Black Furies, Silver Fangs) vampire is unnatural because he lived as human and now breaked the circle. He exist in his unlife. And in their view it is unnatural. He is opposed to life, maby to Wyld.<br /> Other examples mentioned before - of course smell of wyrm. They are mostly evil. Corrupted. Dead. Like parasites on humanity. Human are the children of Weaver and for example Glass Walkers defended them. But of course city dwelling garou have to struggle against influence of vampires. Sometimes they have to cooperate againts bigger evil. It's complicated. It's not black and white, WoD have many shades of gray and that make the settng so good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T04:16:45-07:00","id":1092302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>werewolf43</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052686-garou-and-vampires?p=1092294#post1092294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm In my opinion every tribe have something against leeches in some ways so Garou nation has. The best sample - Shadow Lords. Vampires infested their homeland and lords had to defend themselves, maby their kinfolk. Tzimisce are tough fiends so I guess the war never ended. For example tribes that defend Wyld, creator, life (Red Talons, Black Furies, Silver Fangs) vampire is unnatural because he lived as human and now breaked the circle. He exist in his unlife. And in their view it is unnatural. He is opposed to life, maby to Wyld.<br /> Other examples mentioned before - of course smell of wyrm. They are mostly evil. Corrupted. Dead. Like parasites on humanity. Human are the children of Weaver and for example Glass Walkers defended them. But of course city dwelling garou have to struggle against influence of vampires. Sometimes they have to cooperate againts bigger evil. It's complicated. It's not black and white, WoD have many shades of gray and that make the settng so good.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the case of vampires and Garou, I very much have the view the undead have a strong case of being the Tau in the werewolves' personal Imperium of Mankind. The Garou, ideologically, are committed to the destruction of all Wyrm tainted monstrosities in the world. Vampires, according to Garou religion, are undead corpses inhabited by Banes who prey on the living and stink of the Wyrm as well as the Weaver. They have been historically the enemy of the Garou in many regions with particularly powerful ones capable of raining all sorts of unholy hell down on them through their mortal contacts.<br /> <br /> HOWEVER, then we get to the Tau issue, which is the fact the vampires don't play by the werewolf playbook. Not in the context of not being parasites and monsters. They are, for the most part, very much a bunch of bad guys. It's the fact that vampires really are just the Diet Coke of EvilTM in the World of Darkness as far as the Garou are concerned. It's hard for V:TM players to accept and certainly the Sabbat makes up for it but for the Garou who deal with supernaturals who are 24/7 devoted to kicking dogs/wolves the average vampire doesn't really warrant much attention. The majority of them feed on humans without killing THAT many and spend their lives selfishly accumulating power. Which is bad, yes, but not what everyone else is doing in trying to bring about the end of the world.<br /> <br /> You leave a 100 Formori or Wyrm cultsits alone and the city will get turned into the source of the next Black Plague or a demon summoned which will require the Garou to stop it lest a new Word War break out. You leave a 100 vampires alone in the city and you have a spike in missing persons and a lot of corrupt politicians as well as shady business deals.<br /> <br /> Compared to Black Spiral Dancers, Formori, Pentex, and so on, the undead maintain some trace of restraint or &quot;humanity&quot; (what a stupid word) while holds them back from fully threatening the world. Vampires are also spiritually ignorant to a COLOSSAL degree. While there's only one or two times a Garou will sit down with a Leech to talk to them socially (maybe as part of a dare in Elysium), the fact is they don't know the Wyrm exists and don't believe in him. They actually believe in human religions if they believe in anything at all, which to werewolves is like being a atheist demon or angel. Vampires demons, Garou angels. The vampire population has surged out of control and it would take the entire Garou nation working together simultaneously to &quot;extirpate&quot; them the way Albretch did the Seventh Generation even if that was possible. However, the Garou honestly have bigger problems and vampires are a problem which will keep since, again, they aren't out to bring about the apocalypse.<br /> <br /> It's an attitude that may and probably will change dramatically in any campaign where the Antediluvians are real.<br /> <br /> Until then, the Garou attitude is, &quot;Yeah, we'll kill these guys later.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 05-14-2017, 07:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T06:28:08-07:00","id":1092318,"title":"","content":"Of course, there's always a huge danger of painting the situation with too wide a brush.<br /> <br /> There are vast differences between clans, sects, local politics, and even individuals. There's going to be a huge difference in the way a Silent Strider reacts to a Follower of Set that sold Blood Magic'd drugs to his Kinfolk kid than a Glass Walker running into a Ventrue covering up a Masquarade violation. <br /> <br /> Heck, even the Sabbat knows the danger of infernalism and ancient horrors waking up to eat the world, and if a Baali and a BSD start to cooperate in waking up an Earthbound, it might well take Tzimisce and Shadow Lords working together to stop them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5818-eviltyger","name":"EvilTyger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T09:17:59-07:00","id":1092351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EvilTyger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052686-garou-and-vampires?p=1092318#post1092318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Heck, even the Sabbat knows the danger of infernalism and ancient horrors waking up to eat the world, and if a Baali and a BSD start to cooperate in waking up an Earthbound, it might well take Tzimisce and Shadow Lords working together to stop them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ehhhh.... from a metaphysical perspective, the Baali/Dancers are a bunch of tainted horrors serving a giant bane spirit... which is bad. Conversely, the Tzimisce serve Kupala... which makes them *also* a bunch of tainted horrors serving a giant bane spirit. Zero sum game. The Shadow Lords might try to pit the two Wyrm-aligned groups against each other, but actively aiding either one over the other doesn't make much sense, unless it is in the very, <i>very </i>short term.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3695,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","user":"The Laughing Stranger","date":". 05-14-2017, 12:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T10:16:46-07:00","id":1092362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EvilTyger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052686-garou-and-vampires?p=1092318#post1092318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> There's going to be a huge difference in the way a Silent Strider reacts to a Follower of Set that sold Blood Magic'd drugs to his Kinfolk kid than a Glass Walker running into a Ventrue covering up a Masquarade violation.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've been thinking recently that they should make a TV-series about a Technocrat, a Glass Walker and a Ventrue working together to cover up secrecy breaches (and solving other mysterious and exciting cases!). It is as if I can almost hear and see the opening montage...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T18:56:10-07:00","id":1092618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052686-garou-and-vampires?p=1092351#post1092351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ehhhh.... from a metaphysical perspective, the Baali/Dancers are a bunch of tainted horrors serving a giant bane spirit... which is bad. Conversely, the Tzimisce serve Kupala... which makes them *also* a bunch of tainted horrors serving a giant bane spirit. Zero sum game. The Shadow Lords might try to pit the two Wyrm-aligned groups against each other, but actively aiding either one over the other doesn't make much sense, unless it is in the very, <i>very </i>short term.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thought that was 'Old Clan' and was one of the reasons the ones that formed the Sabbat killed their Anti?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5818-eviltyger","name":"EvilTyger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T21:11:18-07:00","id":1092651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EvilTyger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052686-garou-and-vampires?p=1092618#post1092618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thought that was 'Old Clan' and was one of the reasons the ones that formed the Sabbat killed their Anti?</div> </div> </div> </div>Modern Sabbat aren't the sharpest tools in the drawer. Most would scoff at the idea there's a God who cursed Caine, let alone demon (Wyrm Incarnae?) living under Transylvania.<br /> <br /> Still, most Tzimisce wouldn't serve Kupala.<br /> <br /> As that is, definitely, under the &quot;No Infernalism&quot; rule.<br /> <br /> Not that most Garou or Sabbat would stop to chat about it as the Garou still consider them Wyrm creatures and the Sabbat consider werewolves threats to their territory.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-15T07:23:14-07:00","id":1092792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052686-garou-and-vampires?p=1092651#post1092651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Modern Sabbat aren't the sharpest tools in the drawer. Most would scoff at the idea there's a God who cursed Caine, let alone demon (Wyrm Incarnae?) living under Transylvania.<br /> <br /> Still, most Tzimisce wouldn't serve Kupala.<br /> <br /> As that is, definitely, under the &amp;quot;No Infernalism&amp;quot; rule.<br /> <br /> Not that most Garou or Sabbat would stop to chat about it as the Garou still consider them Wyrm creatures and the Sabbat consider werewolves threats to their territory.</div> </div> </div> </div>That particular example was meant to be highly situational and off the beaten track, primarily meant to point out that no matter how much the 'standard' is hate, it doesn't mean that there aren't events that can (at least temporarily) cause goals to align.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5818-eviltyger","name":"EvilTyger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-15T21:04:23-07:00","id":1093093,"title":"","content":"The problem for the Garou is that Kindred can always make more and seem to be eager to make more. Their unnatural reproduction is one of the reasons why the Garou find them so horrific. The idea that one Kindred could literally start a chain reaction that could turn the humans of an entire continent into Kindred within a month probably gives the Garou nightmares. The KJ, despite their inhumanity, are relatively benign by comparison, as they cannot directly transform other people into KJ.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-15T21:15:13-07:00","id":1093095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052686-garou-and-vampires?p=1093093#post1093093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem for the Garou is that Kindred can always make more and seem to be eager to make more. Their unnatural reproduction is one of the reasons why the Garou find them so horrific. The idea that one Kindred could literally start a chain reaction that could turn the humans of an entire continent into Kindred within a month probably gives the Garou nightmares. The KJ, despite their inhumanity, are relatively benign by comparison, as they cannot directly transform other people into KJ.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course, Sabbat aside, vampires understand how stupid this is and practice their own population control.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-16T05:51:52-07:00","id":1093193,"title":"","content":"Of course, but the Garou do not generally run into Kindred who practice population control, they run into Caitiff/Panders who are abandoned after being sired without Cam permission. I would not be surprised if over 90% of the Kindred in the USA were Embraced outside of the Cam, it is just that the ones outside of the Cam probably have an average life expectedly of one month because they come to the attention of the Cam, the Garou, the Hunters, etc before they learn discretion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-17T08:38:16-07:00","id":1093668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052686-garou-and-vampires?p=1093093#post1093093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem for the Garou is that Kindred can always make more and seem to be eager to make more. Their unnatural reproduction is one of the reasons why the Garou find them so horrific. The idea that one Kindred could literally start a chain reaction that could turn the humans of an entire continent into Kindred within a month probably gives the Garou nightmares. The KJ, despite their inhumanity, are relatively benign by comparison, as they cannot directly transform other people into KJ.</div> </div> </div> </div>An entire continent? Seems unlikely for a number of reasons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","name":"Monalfie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12552_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-17T08:54:36-07:00","id":1093672,"title":"","content":"If a 5th generation Kindred embraces two people every night, if the resulting 6th generation Kindred embraces two people every night, etc, one 5th generation Kindred can start a chain reaction that could convert an entire continent in a month.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-17T09:44:37-07:00","id":1093685,"title":"","content":"It's like when any supernatural tries to conquer the world with magic. It's feasible in theory, but you are going to be stopped by one force or another.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-17T10:18:54-07:00","id":1093693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052686-garou-and-vampires?p=1093672#post1093672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a 5th generation Kindred embraces two people every night, if the resulting 6th generation Kindred embraces two people every night, etc, one 5th generation Kindred can start a chain reaction that could convert an entire continent in a month.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that they also require time to learn disciplines and a source of food.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5818-eviltyger","name":"EvilTyger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-17T11:19:44-07:00","id":1093711,"title":"","content":"Dont forget the SAD Probaly has contingency plans for just this kind of thing, likely so does pentex... possibly even the technocracy.<br /> <br /> I could see them changing over a dozen people a night at the start of the chain...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-17T12:30:22-07:00","id":1093738,"title":"","content":"Even if it is infeasible, the Garou still fear that sort of thing, as they do not want billions of superpowered fomori (in their interpretation) running around. Better for the Garou to kill the Kindred when they find them rather than let things explode out of control. The fact that the Anarchs and Sabbat bear most of the Garou attacks is a happy coincidence for the Cam and the Independents.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-17T13:16:58-07:00","id":1093775,"title":"","content":"You dont think Setites or Baali will be singled out for eradication?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-17T18:10:01-07:00","id":1093925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052686-garou-and-vampires?p=1093738#post1093738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even if it is infeasible, the Garou still fear that sort of thing, as they do not want billions of superpowered fomori (in their interpretation) running around. Better for the Garou to kill the Kindred when they find them rather than let things explode out of control. The fact that the Anarchs and Sabbat bear most of the Garou attacks is a happy coincidence for the Cam and the Independents.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then the Garou would probably go extinct. They could wipe out the Kindred but....well, that was millennium ago. Doing so now would deplete their strength to the point of losing to every other enemy actually trying to bring about the world's end.<br /> <br /> Not that the Kindred would win either as such a war would destroy the Masquerade and result in their extermination by mortals.<br /> <br /> Garou, at least, can hide from them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 05-17-2017, 09:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-17T20:23:53-07:00","id":1093963,"title":"","content":"The Garou are killing Kindred everyday without losing any sleep, and the Kindred are terrified by the Garou because a pack of Garou can easily kill off the entire Kindred population of a metropolitan area if the local Kindred are not discrete (and if they give the Garou enough reason to bother to hunt them down). The Garou do not really fear what the Kindred can do to them (other than the Embrace), they fear what the Kindred can do to their Kin. While there are exceptions, the majority of the Garou think that the only good Kindred is a dead Kindred and, as long as it is occurring to another faction, the majority of the Kindred are willing to cheer them on from a hypothetically safe distance.<br /> <br /> The reason why the Camarilla tends to do better with the Garou than other Kindred groups is that they are generally willing to keep their distance from the Garou. The Sabbat tends to be too arrogant and the Anarchs tend to be too ignorant. In the view of the Camarilla, every Sabbat member killed by the Garou is a Sabbat stronghold that is just a little weaker and every Anarch member killed by the Garou is just one more competitor removed from the equation. Heck, I bet that the majority of Princes do not terribly care if the Garou kill off any Caitiff in their territory because the Garou are just saving them the effort (and the Caitiff are providing a valuable service by allowing the Garou to believe they killed off the local Kindred threat).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-17T20:30:08-07:00","id":1093965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052686-garou-and-vampires?p=1093963#post1093963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Garou are killing Kindred everyday without losing any sleep.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on how you handle it but I generally rule when Garou kill a low status vampire, it gets ignored. Because vampires love getting rid of problems.<br /> <br /> If they kill someone who matters though, there's retaliation.<br /> <br /> If the Garou retaliate, it gets ugly.<br /> <br /> Which is why most Garou don't do causal vampire hunting in my games.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-17T20:39:31-07:00","id":1093968,"title":"","content":"Vampire hunting is just like fomori hunting in my games except Kindred are not active during the day. If Kindred are too arrogant or too ignorant to avoid Garou, they usually end up dead. Camarilla Elders just know how to avoid drawing attention to themselves and use their Disciplines to make sure that the Garou do not follow them home during the day. The Garou just have too many advantages over the Kindred if the Kindred decide to flout the Masquerade, which is one of the reasons that the Camarilla succeeds where other groups of Kindred fail.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T19:50:04-07:00","id":1094395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052686-garou-and-vampires?p=1093968#post1093968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampire hunting is just like fomori hunting in my games except Kindred are not active during the day. If Kindred are too arrogant or too ignorant to avoid Garou, they usually end up dead. Camarilla Elders just know how to avoid drawing attention to themselves and use their Disciplines to make sure that the Garou do not follow them home during the day. The Garou just have too many advantages over the Kindred if the Kindred decide to flout the Masquerade, which is one of the reasons that the Camarilla succeeds where other groups of Kindred fail.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think vampires generally are the kind of people who engage werewolves in combat. Anarchs and Sabbat? Yes, which is why they're a special kind of stupid but they also travel in packs so they have a chance of doing damage. Generally, I tend to think when werewolves are at &quot;war&quot; with vampires, the vampires handle matters by ghouling a bunch of people with military grade weapons and then dominating them before handing out silver bullets. They then try and ambush the Garou's kinfolk and threaten their holy places. Maybe attack whatever mortal resources they have. You know, basically Pentex lite.<br /> <br /> It's not like finding vampires is easy too.<br /> <br /> In other words, Garou CAN mess up vampires real bad but it's going to be costly and annoying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T20:30:32-07:00","id":1094404,"title":"","content":"Smart Kindred ghost when Garou come sniffing around. They drink animal blood or keep to their Herds, they do business through their ghouls, or they go visit friends in other cities. Garou have better things to do than wait a few weeks for Kindred to appear out of nowhere. It is only when Kindred are careless or stupid that Garou know that they are around.<br /> <br /> Honestly, there are so few Garou in an average city that the chances are quite low that they will stumble across Kindred who maintain the Masquerade. In fact, a local Garou pack is good protection against Anarchs and/or Sabbat because they will always draw the attention of the Garou. The Cam Kindred go on vacation for a few weeks and, when they come back, the interlopers are dead, the Garou once again think they have gotten rid of the Kindred in the city, and the Cam Kindred gets to party without worrying about either group.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-27T20:52:33-07:00","id":1097680,"title":"","content":"There was a discussion about this back when KotEK came out, as the Bastet book mentioned a war between the Simba and the Kindred. Mostly, Kindred are going to get out of the way. They have the potential to live a very long time, and the idea of getting in the way of powerful werecreatures (some of whom can harness sunlight and fire) tends to lessen that potential. The result being that that 'war' wound up thinning the lesser vampires of the region.<br /> <br /> So in an odd way, the Kindred best able to protect themselves the least likely to need to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5818-eviltyger","name":"EvilTyger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T03:34:36-07:00","id":1097731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052686-garou-and-vampires?p=1094395#post1094395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think vampires generally are the kind of people who engage werewolves in combat. Anarchs and Sabbat? Yes, which is why they're a special kind of stupid but they also travel in packs so they have a chance of doing damage. Generally, I tend to think when werewolves are at &quot;war&quot; with vampires, the vampires handle matters by ghouling a bunch of people with military grade weapons and then dominating them before handing out silver bullets. They then try and ambush the Garou's kinfolk and threaten their holy places. Maybe attack whatever mortal resources they have. You know, basically Pentex lite.<br /> <br /> It's not like finding vampires is easy too.<br /> <br /> In other words, Garou CAN mess up vampires real bad but it's going to be costly and annoying.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thing is Vampires don't really know much about these things. Vampires rarely even know a Lupine has a human Identity. I really don't see vampires doing an eye for an eye with Lupines, especially not the Camarilla. So Unless an entire city is in danger of being genocided by Lupines they would likely find a suitable scapegoat among their court to punish, and try to lie low. Vampires in general keep that eye for an eye stuff for dealing with other Cainites, and humans, if brought into a blood feud with another supernatural they are usually not happy and the local population either has the Prince bring back peace and safety or they lynch the prince. That is a Princes main goal, safety and food for his territory. In General Ghouling and Silver bullets is a defense measure because they don't know where to ambush, unless they know they can ambush peace deal or something.<br /> <br /> And its not so much the point Vampires don't go hunting for Werewolves Personally, the thing is they know they have to wipe them out completely if they bring on a war because Werewolves appear out of nowhere, have weird powers that they can't predict, and have a tendency to somehow (spirits) find the Masters of the Ghouls they just killed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":754,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","user":"Eldagusto","date":".  left out a paragraph 05-28-2017, 06:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T06:24:40-07:00","id":1097761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052686-garou-and-vampires?p=1097731#post1097731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thing is Vampires don't really know much about these things. Vampires rarely even know a Lupine has a human Identity. I really don't see vampires doing an eye for an eye with Lupines, especially not the Camarilla. So Unless an entire city is in danger of being genocided by Lupines they would likely find a suitable scapegoat among their court to punish, and try to lie low. Vampires in general keep that eye for an eye stuff for dealing with other Cainites, and humans, if brought into a blood feud with another supernatural they are usually not happy and the local population either has the Prince bring back peace and safety or they lynch the prince. That is a Princes main goal, safety and food for his territory. In General Ghouling and Silver bullets is a defense measure because they don't know where to ambush, unless they know they can ambush peace deal or something.<br /> <br /> And its not so much the point Vampires don't go hunting for Werewolves Personally, the thing is they know they have to wipe them out completely if they bring on a war because Werewolves appear out of nowhere, have weird powers that they can't predict, and have a tendency to somehow (spirits) find the Masters of the Ghouls they just killed.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a difference between what the average Kindred on the street knows about Garou and the Prince of the City as well as the authorities of the Camarilla. Mind you, no vampire has probably ever made an extensive study of Garou religious beliefs (and lived to tell the tale) but I imagine they have the basics of what you'd find in the back of &quot;Vampire: The Masquerade&quot; down. I.e. silver, werewolves are born not made, they have families, tribal structures, and so on. After all, in Under a Blood Red Moon, the Sabbat knows enough to target Kinfolk families. Same holds true for Garou. Undead, fire, sunlight, infect by biting, and have blood addicted slaves.<br /> <br /> The idea Princes will ignore threats to their position is also something I don't necessarily think holds either.<br /> <br /> Garou and Vampires don't really clash that often because Garou are rural and Vampires are urban with the two urban Garou knowing not to mess with them (they have bigger problems) not because the vampires back down or vice versa.<br /> <br /> We also know it's still canon there are places where werewolves and vampires fight ala Milwaukee.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T07:28:05-07:00","id":1097766,"title":"","content":"Camarilla Princes know that their members just have to lie low for a few weeks when there are Garou around. They make sure that the local members keep to animal blood and the blood of their Herds while a local pack of Garou annihilates every Anarch, Caitiff, Sabbat, etc in the area. By the time that the Garou go back to the woods, most of the Camarilla Kindred competitors are gone, so having a local pack of Garou go on a killing spree every decade of so is actually beneficial to local Kindred who keep the Masquerade.<br /> <br /> Kindred survive through subtlety and discretion because, with the except of the Methuselah, they are barracudas, not sharks. Barracudas thrive when they keep out of the way of sharks, just as Kindred thrive when they keep out of the way of Garou. Kindred, especially neonates, end up as corpses when they try to go toe-to-toe with Garou, but so does anything that is not designed to be a Garou killer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T10:35:01-07:00","id":1097819,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052686-garou-and-vampires?p=1097766#post1097766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Camarilla Princes know that their members just have to lie low for a few weeks when there are Garou around. They make sure that the local members keep to animal blood and the blood of their Herds while a local pack of Garou annihilates every Anarch, Caitiff, Sabbat, etc in the area. By the time that the Garou go back to the woods, most of the Camarilla Kindred competitors are gone, so having a local pack of Garou go on a killing spree every decade of so is actually beneficial to local Kindred who keep the Masquerade.<br /> <br /> Kindred survive through subtlety and discretion because, with the except of the Methuselah, they are barracudas, not sharks. Barracudas thrive when they keep out of the way of sharks, just as Kindred thrive when they keep out of the way of Garou. Kindred, especially neonates, end up as corpses when they try to go toe-to-toe with Garou, but so does anything that is not designed to be a Garou killer.</div> </div> </div> </div>The idea Princes don't kill Garou ALL THE TIME seems like a really big assumption.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T11:04:33-07:00","id":1097828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052686-garou-and-vampires?p=1097819#post1097819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The idea Princes don't kill Garou ALL THE TIME seems like a really big assumption.</div> </div> </div> </div>So is the notion that they do. Who wants to risk their centuries of existence by calling down the murdericane that is the werewolves when they can just lay low and let time take care of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13009,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","user":"BurritoMage","date":". 05-28-2017, 02:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T13:23:56-07:00","id":1097860,"title":"","content":"Since we are talking about Garou as opposed to Lupines, because this is the WtA forum, the worst thing that the Kindred can do is call attention to themselves by trying to hunt Garou. Garou do not have to worry about Humanity or Conscience, so they can slaughter Ghouls and Kindred from dusk till dawn without blinking an eye. Yes, the Kindred can ambush the first Garou but, after killing one of them, they have to deal with the entire flipping Garou Nation, which is not going to tolerate Kindred killing Garou. They will purge the area of anything resembling the Kindred and that will be that. It is one of the reasons why smart Princes forbid engagement against the Garou.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-29T04:22:35-07:00","id":1098058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052686-garou-and-vampires?p=1097860#post1097860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since we are talking about Garou as opposed to Lupines, because this is the WtA forum, the worst thing that the Kindred can do is call attention to themselves by trying to hunt Garou. Garou do not have to worry about Humanity or Conscience, so they can slaughter Ghouls and Kindred from dusk till dawn without blinking an eye. Yes, the Kindred can ambush the first Garou but, after killing one of them, they have to deal with the entire flipping Garou Nation, which is not going to tolerate Kindred killing Garou. They will purge the area of anything resembling the Kindred and that will be that. It is one of the reasons why smart Princes forbid engagement against the Garou.</div> </div> </div> </div>This being W:TA and not V:TM, that would turn into an enormous disaster because the Garou are a race constantly at each other's throats and fully willing to slash each other to pieces over the slightest insults. Also, the fact they have no humanity is a WEAKNESS rather than a flaw as the main problem of the modern day is the Garou have no method of dealing with problems other than ATTACK ATTACK ATTACK.<br /> <br /> The idea the Garou would band together as a nation is ludicrous as they can't even do that when Baba Yaga TAKES OVER RUSSIA. Hell, a good third of the Garou were willing to join her.<br /> <br /> You have a very rose-tinted view of the Garou vs. Vampires which I think undermines both as if the Garou can just steamroll vampires, then where's the Glory? Where's the Renown? Treating vampires as easy prey kind of makes the Garou look lesser for hunting them.<br /> <br /> Why not let vampires vs. werewolves be a fight?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-29T05:00:59-07:00","id":1098067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052686-garou-and-vampires?p=1098058#post1098058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also, the fact they have no humanity is a WEAKNESS<br /> <br /> modern day is the Garou have no method of dealing with problems other than ATTACK ATTACK ATTACK.<br /> <br /> The idea the Garou would band together as a nation is ludicrous</div> </div> </div> </div>1. that's a weakness why? 'Humanity' is a completely artificial invention of the game developers. Garou have their own version of it in Harmony. That human's aren't a central focus of it doesn't make it's morality any less viable. Yeah they give no f*cks over dusting a walking cannibal corpse, I neither. <br /> <br /> 2. I think that it's more that Vamps have no idea they are fighting werewolves till they go 'ATTACK ATTACK ATTACK'<br /> <br /> 3. 100% true. There is no Garou Nation in anything more but name. Getting even a single tribe to act in unison is a nightmare.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-29T06:25:30-07:00","id":1098086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Warpwind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052686-garou-and-vampires?p=1098067#post1098067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1. that's a weakness why? 'Humanity' is a completely artificial invention of the game developers. Garou have their own version of it in Harmony. That human's aren't a central focus of it doesn't make it's morality any less viable. Yeah they give no f*cks over dusting a walking cannibal corpse, I neither.<br /> <br /> 2. I think that it's more that Vamps have no idea they are fighting werewolves till they go 'ATTACK ATTACK ATTACK'<br /> <br /> 3. 100% true. There is no Garou Nation in anything more but name. Getting even a single tribe to act in unison is a nightmare.</div> </div> </div> </div>1. Basically, because the problems of the modern era are ones which require Garou to deal with humanity and through humanity. I'm not talking about the fact humanity as a moral system is somehow superior to others. I'm saying humanity as a concept is something Garou need to be able to relate to and through in order to deal with humans in a way they can save the environment/defeat Pentex/reform to save Gaia. Basically, Garou morality with its exaltation of violence and power and dominance is something that resulted in the War of Rage and Imperium and they've never really learned their lesson. It's not working anymore because we're out of the caves and into the cities.<br /> <br /> It's why the Children of Gaia have somewhat of the right idea (even if they take it too far) and Stargazers too.<br /> <br /> You need humanity to be able to work with humanity and unfortunately (for Garou) humanity is the only way to win. The Red Talons plan of murdering 90% of us isn't going to work.<br /> <br /> 2. The lack of subtlety among the Garou is part of the issues. Vampires are extremely well-adapted to city life and watching for supernatural events so when Garou go on killing sprees and its caught on film or a Metis corpse gets left behind, the vampires will probably hear about it second. Mind you, this is only true in an integrated World of Darkness.<br /> <br /> Which many Werewolf STs may dislike.<br /> <br /> 3. Like herding wolves. Except wolves get along better. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-29T08:27:25-07:00","id":1098106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052686-garou-and-vampires?p=1098086#post1098086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1. Basically, because the problems of the modern era are ones which require Garou to deal with humanity and through humanity. I'm not talking about the fact humanity as a moral system is somehow superior to others. I'm saying humanity as a concept is something Garou need to be able to relate to and through in order to deal with humans in a way they can save the environment/defeat Pentex/reform to save Gaia. Basically, Garou morality with its exaltation of violence and power and dominance is something that resulted in the War of Rage and Imperium and they've never really learned their lesson. It's not working anymore because we're out of the caves and into the cities.<br /> <br /> It's why the Children of Gaia have somewhat of the right idea (even if they take it too far) and Stargazers too.<br /> <br /> You need humanity to be able to work with humanity and unfortunately (for Garou) humanity is the only way to win. The Red Talons plan of murdering 90% of us isn't going to work.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, see, that stat is an arbitrary one meant solely for vampires and other characters on a downward spiral from the moment of their transformation from normal humans into monsters. Its absence in Werewolf doesn't really hamper anything; the presence of Rage is another matter. Witness also how Kinfolk characters don't have a Humanity track, either. It's because the game isn't there to track your degeneration. It's there to celebrate the times that you managed to rise above, in the form of non-Glory Renown and having friends and family who aren't dead.<br /> <br /> I mean, Glass Walkers don't have any problems working through modern means. They bend the spirits of technology to their whims. Werewolves cannot be truly gentle as such, or completely non-threatening all the time, but they can be clever...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2. The lack of subtlety among the Garou is part of the issues. Vampires are extremely well-adapted to city life </div> </div> </div>If they were known, the humans around them would drag them into the streets to burn. They're walking a tightrope in exchange for easy access to blood.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> and watching for supernatural events so when Garou go on killing sprees and its caught on film or a Metis corpse gets left behind, the vampires will probably hear about it second. Mind you, this is only true in an integrated World of Darkness.<br /> <br /> Which many Werewolf STs may dislike. </div> </div> </div>No, metis corpses are always a threat to the Veil unless some means have been used to make sure, ahead of time, that they end up in other forms if it happens. You may be significantly overestimating the number of killing sprees that Garou go on, though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3. Like herding wolves. Except wolves get along better. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> </div> </div> </div>On some levels, yes. They don't get that pack attack coordination by totem, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-29T08:37:19-07:00","id":1098108,"title":"","content":"Baba Yaga is a 8,000 year old Methuselah who controls armies of banes, fomori, Kindred, etc. The reason why the Garou were unwilling to go after her was that it would have taken such a large population of Garou to chew through her army that the forces of the Wyrm would have surged everywhere else. That is different from having few dozen scrub Kindred killing a Garou and declaring their territory a 'kill zone' for Garou. The former is a matter of practicality (Baba Yaga is one of a dozens of Big Bads that the Garou are aware of and the Garou have to use a cost-benefit analysis when dealing with Big Bads), the latter is a matter of honor (the Garou cannot go about their tasks if every scrub Kindred thinks they can collect a wolf pelt). While the Garou might avoid Baba Yaga because they do not want to be decimated during their battle against her, they are not worried about a few dozen lucky scrub Kindred.<br /> <br /> When it comes to beginning characters, beginning Garou trump beginning Kindred. Beginning Garou are capable of going out during the day, beginning Garou can summon legions of spirits to help them in their conflicts, beginning Garou soak aggravated damage with full Stamina outside of breed form, beginning Garou regenerate without spending anything outside of breed form, beginning Garou turn into 8' tall murder machines, etc. Since the vast majority of Kindred die within the first ten years of existence, the average Kindred will never catch up with the average Garou because Garou will always be better than Kindred of the same level of experience.<br /> <br /> Of course, ancient Kindred are a horse of a different color and, after a thousand years of existence, ancient Kindred are capable of winning a fight against any single Garou. However, ancient Kindred are wise enough not to hunt Garou because Garou rarely come alone, and they have better things to do with their immortality than risk it by kicking the hornets nest that is the Garou Nation. Even if they kill one of the Garou, the rest of the Garou in the area will temporarily put aside their grievances to ash the ancient Kindred, much like Appalachian Mountain Clans used to stand united against outsiders but would fight tooth-and-nail against each other when they were left alone.<br /> <br /> On another note, Garou really do not suffer from any particular disadvantages in modern society (at least not compared to Kindred). On the first point, 80%-88% of Garou are Homid, so they were born and raised among humans, so they are capable of fitting in without issue as long as they do not develop excessive rage (anything above Rage 5 is probably going to have a Garou relegated to combat roles such as Caern protection and Umbral strikes). On the second point, Garou do not really have to worry about getting caught on film because 1) the majority of Garou do not have high enough Rage where they will go berserk at a drop of a hat, 2) there are even odds that a Garou will run away as they will enter into a berserk frenzy, 3) they look like any other human when they are not shapeshifting, 4) they have common Gifts that torch technology or that hide them from people, and 5) the majority of humans will be running away screaming due to the Delirium instead of snapping photos when they witness a 8' tall murder machine. On the third point, Garou tend to stand united against outsiders, even if they fight each other to the death over minor points of honor when they are not facing an immediate external threat (the other shapeshifters wish that the Garou did not stand together quite so well against external threats).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-29T10:25:56-07:00","id":1098139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052686-garou-and-vampires?p=1098106#post1098106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...the game isn't there to track your degeneration. It's there to celebrate the times that you managed to rise above, in the form of non-Glory Renown and having friends and family who aren't dead.</div> </div> </div> </div>Preach.<br /> Different game lines, different stories being told.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-29T10:32:25-07:00","id":1098144,"title":"","content":"have to agree with @Aya_Tari here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4340,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","user":"Warpwind","date":". 05-29-2017, 03:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-29T10:54:34-07:00","id":1098150,"title":"","content":"Personally, I have always seen vampire hunting as something extra the garou do, rather than something resources are put into. There are tribes such as Silent Striders, Shadows Lords and Silver Fangs who have an ancestral duty to it. But to an Uktena or a Fianna, vampires are basically one more Wyrm-monster in the list. One that isn't -as- troublesome as fomori or banes, since some actually know how to behave and don't hurt people.<br /> <br /> Any larger scale vampire hunting is either by Striders or Lords, or is strictly case by case basis. Otherwise, vampires just aren't that big of a worry to the garou when there are bigger things to deal with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-29T11:17:39-07:00","id":1098160,"title":"","content":"Oh, I agree, and I think that part of the reason for that is that elder Kindred know better than to pick fights with the Garou.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-29T13:47:15-07:00","id":1098221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052686-garou-and-vampires?p=1098150#post1098150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any larger scale vampire hunting is either by Striders or Lords, or is strictly case by case basis. Otherwise, vampires just aren't that big of a worry to the garou when there are bigger things to deal with.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Silent Striders have always been a special case. Their hatred for vampires is because the Cult of Setekh and their dead god caused them to lose <b><i>major</i></b> face in front of the other Garou, Owl and Gaia by driving them out of the lands they were charged with overseeing. It's a hardcore old school vendetta driven by a level of anger (Rage) that is totally unknown to the average human. I think only the Bubasti can really understand how it impacted them. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-29T14:01:49-07:00","id":1098228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052686-garou-and-vampires?p=1098221#post1098221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Silent Striders have always been a special case. Their hatred for vampires is because the Cult of Setekh and their dead god caused them to lose <b><i>major</i></b> face in front of the other Garou, Owl and Gaia by driving them out of the lands they were charged with overseeing. It's a hardcore old school vendetta driven by a level of anger (Rage) that is totally unknown to the average human. I think only the Bubasti can really understand how it impacted them.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Shadow Lords too, since they and Tzimisce have basically been fighting over the same area for eons. Enough that seeing Camazotz in crinos was an automatic &quot;oh no, they are HERE too!?&quot; from them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-29T18:52:33-07:00","id":1098310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052686-garou-and-vampires?p=1098108#post1098108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Baba Yaga is a 8,000 year old Methuselah who controls armies of banes, fomori, Kindred, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ultimately, those were chaff that the Garou could have easily sliced through in relatively little time, or at least far less time than the prime threats. The problem came from the Zmei and Bezariel, which demand far more focused expertise, among other strengths, to tackle. Also, both are the result of magical bindings not of vampires; the Zmei were summoned and bound to Baba Yaga when she was fighting against the Embrace and, I guess from the way the tale is told, not quite a vampire yet. The Blood Angel, meanwhile, was called forth by a ghouled and blood bound Chorister.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-29T19:02:31-07:00","id":1098313,"title":"","content":"While Baba Yaga is probably the most powerful of Methuselah, I do not think that any member of the 4th generation is a push over (with the exception of the Giovanni and the Tremere). With an average of 4,000 years of experience, any active 4th generation Methuselah is a match for practically anything in cWoD. At best, you are talking about a creature with +45 Attributes, +200 Abilities, +63 Disciplines, and +63 Freebie Points. And we really do not know how many of them are out there because Obfuscate 9 allows them to trick everything but Auspex 9 (and similarly stupidly powerful abililties). There could be a ninety-one (seven per Clan) or a thirteen hundred (one hundred per Clan). Only the 3rd generation knows how many were sired and they are not speaking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-29T19:48:45-07:00","id":1098323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Warpwind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052686-garou-and-vampires?p=1098144#post1098144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">have to agree with @Aya_Tari here.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree. Basically, Vampires are just another kind of Pentex to Garou and we know Pentex is kicking the crap out of the Garou as well as humanity. Mind you, if Pentex (or vampires) win, it's the end of the world so that's not a good thing for them either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-29T20:05:44-07:00","id":1098329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052686-garou-and-vampires?p=1098323#post1098323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I disagree. Basically, Vampires are just another kind of Pentex to Garou and we know Pentex is kicking the crap out of the Garou as well as humanity. Mind you, if Pentex (or vampires) win, it's the end of the world so that's not a good thing for them either.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except vampires don't have the goal of corrupting the world for their insane god. Can you tell me what exactly the end game of the vampires is that's so world ending?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-29T20:33:09-07:00","id":1098332,"title":"","content":"And Kindred do not make a million neonates (or ghouls) a year while Pentex needs to make a million fomori a year just to keep up with the attrition from Bane possession and the conflicts with the Fera.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-29T21:19:54-07:00","id":1098343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052686-garou-and-vampires?p=1098323#post1098323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I disagree. Basically, Vampires are just another kind of Pentex to Garou and we know Pentex is kicking the crap out of the Garou as well as humanity. Mind you, if Pentex (or vampires) win, it's the end of the world so that's not a good thing for them either.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pentex is far more widespread. It lets vampires into the clubhouse on occasion, but probably doesn't feel the need to hold back in competition or opposition. Ultimnately, the vampires would lose, on account of how vulnerable their position is and how much fewer they are than the enemies of the Garou. Because while there might be more vampires than werewolves, there aren't that many werewolves, and their foes tend to be far more numerous even before placing vampires on the scales.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-29T22:02:55-07:00","id":1098349,"title":"","content":"Vampires are a symptom (not the cause) of the oncoming Apocalypse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-29T23:59:46-07:00","id":1098362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052686-garou-and-vampires?p=1098323#post1098323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I disagree. Basically, Vampires are just another kind of Pentex to Garou and we know Pentex is kicking the crap out of the Garou as well as humanity. Mind you, if Pentex (or vampires) win, it's the end of the world so that's not a good thing for them either.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say garou have far more vampire lore than Pentex lore, having dealt with the former for centuries. Even if garou don't understand vampires, they still have a much better idea how vampires behave than how Pentex does. And vampires aren't actively TRYING to make things worse, like Pentex is. So vampires can be left in peace somewhat, until they become a problem.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-30T05:28:33-07:00","id":1098412,"title":"","content":"In my opinion, most Kindred do not want to become a problem for the Garou. I think that the majority of Kindred would be happy if the Garou believed that the Kindred went extinct. Due to the effects of the Masquerade, most Garou probably think that the Kindred are an endangered species that they are only happy to help to extinction when they come across one of the rare examples of Kindred.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-30T07:05:30-07:00","id":1098420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052686-garou-and-vampires?p=1098412#post1098412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my opinion, most Kindred do not want to become a problem for the Garou. I think that the majority of Kindred would be happy if the Garou believed that the Kindred went extinct. Due to the effects of the Masquerade, most Garou probably think that the Kindred are an endangered species that they are only happy to help to extinction when they come across one of the rare examples of Kindred.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think most Kindred believe everywhere outside of a city is infested with Garou from the descriptions in the back of the book and most Garou believe cities are infested with Leeches. I think both races encounter each other all of the time because they're the two most numerous supernatural factions as well as predominate in the setting. That's not excluding the fact the Sabbat exists for the purpose of proving itself via war and wouldn't remotely back down from any conflicts with the Garou or try to &quot;ignore&quot; attacks on their own kind like you claim the undead would.<br /> <br /> No, mind you, neither side PREDOMINATELY considers the other to be a primary enemy but in any setting where they are both &quot;canon&quot; then they will have an uneasy balance of power.<br /> <br /> I say that as a person who thinks the Garou and vampires fighting was cool well before Underworld ruined it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-30T09:26:47-07:00","id":1098453,"title":"","content":"I am not quite sure if encounters are that common though. If you assume ratios of 1:50,000 Kindred and 1:250,000 Garou in the USA and Canada, the odds are slim for random encounters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-30T15:37:05-07:00","id":1098586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052686-garou-and-vampires?p=1098323#post1098323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I disagree. Basically, Vampires are just another kind of Pentex to Garou and we know Pentex is kicking the crap out of the Garou as well as humanity. Mind you, if Pentex (or vampires) win, it's the end of the world so that's not a good thing for them either.</div> </div> </div> </div>What do you think a Vampire &quot;win&quot; looks like? I'm genuinely curious (and is this from the WtA,&quot;Leech&quot; perspective or a VtM. Vampire one).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052686-garou-and-vampires?p=1098412#post1098412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my opinion, most Kindred do not want to become a problem for the Garou. I think that the majority of Kindred would be happy if the Garou believed that the Kindred went extinct. Due to the effects of the Masquerade, most Garou probably think that the Kindred are an endangered species that they are only happy to help to extinction when they come across one of the rare examples of Kindred.</div> </div> </div> </div>I certainly don't think Garou perceive kindred as a sort of endangered species. Whether or not the real numbers support it I agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a>, that the Garou think that the cities are infested with leeches. The fluff in the Antagonists section generally support this view.<br /> <br /> Mind you, I disagree with Aya's assessment that the Camarilla handles Garou better than other factions. I think in general smart Vampires lay low if Garou are on a warpath (incredibly rare in general) and individuals generally just vacate the area if they spot a werewolf first (even Elders). There is just no reason to unnecessarily risk unlife. Garou are unpredictable in what they can do. This is actually somewhat the same from the Garou's point of view, insomuch as they won't pick random fights with Vampires (which seems to be the overwhelming opinion on these forums from my experience). Garou are much more likely to back off and tail the Vampire to an optimal ambush spot to ensure the best chances of success with the least amount of risk. It's not like 1 leech death is worth rending the Veil.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-30T16:51:58-07:00","id":1098612,"title":"","content":"Or a potential ambush. I am sure that elder Kindred have used neonates as bait to lure Garou into a position where the Garou can either a) eliminate another Kindred whom the neonate is innocently taking a message to (a personal foe of their patron) or b) be ambushed by a couple dozen neonates with silver weapons. While it is highly unlikely that modern Kindred would actually want to ambush Garou, it has probably happened enough times over the last one thousand years that Garou are careful when they detect a 'random' Kindred (it probably happened quite a bit during the Dark Ages when Garou and Kindred each had population densities tenfold what they are in modern times and neither group cared as much about avoiding notice from the mortal population).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-30T21:28:50-07:00","id":1098656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052686-garou-and-vampires?p=1098612#post1098612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or a potential ambush. I am sure that elder Kindred have used neonates as bait to lure Garou into a position where the Garou can either a) eliminate another Kindred whom the neonate is innocently taking a message to (a personal foe of their patron) or b) be ambushed by a couple dozen neonates with silver weapons. While it is highly unlikely that modern Kindred would actually want to ambush Garou, it has probably happened enough times over the last one thousand years that Garou are careful when they detect a 'random' Kindred (it probably happened quite a bit during the Dark Ages when Garou and Kindred each had population densities tenfold what they are in modern times and neither group cared as much about avoiding notice from the mortal population).</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh. On the first example (using the Garou tailing a Neonate to eliminate another target), the Elder in question would have to somehow know the Garou were tracking the Neonate (which might actually be impossible for them to do) and try and set up a meeting down the road, and hope the Garou wait long enough in eliminating said Neonate. I don't think it's impossible. Just that there are a lot of variables. For the second one (the ambush with silver), this is probably more likely but Garou can and do survive such ambushes since they can literally teleport out of existence, to say nothing of danger sense altering them beforehand (from the Vampire perspective). So that one isn't worth the risk in general if you can avoid it (as an Elder, imo). I do agree though that things like this have happened over the whole of time, since both sides have a healthy (again, imo) hatred/distrust of the opposing side. <br /> <br /> Both tell tales (as CT pointed out) about how the others infest their home turfs. Even if OOC we know this to be untrue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-30T23:44:35-07:00","id":1098673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052686-garou-and-vampires?p=1098420#post1098420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">. I think both races encounter each other all of the time because they're the two most numerous supernatural factions as well as predominate in the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ghosts are the most numerous supernatural. Probably followed by Numinaed types(Hedge mages, psychics), Changelings have a much larger organization so they SEEM to have much higher numbers. Hell Ghouls/Kinfolk probably out number their respective big splat","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-31T08:06:59-07:00","id":1098770,"title":"","content":"My main objection is the fact Princes only hold their position because they appear tough and are able to hold the Masquerade. It's the vampire mafia meets Feudalism.<br /> <br /> A prince who just lets Garou act with impunity is going to lose his position very quickly.<br /> <br /> Especially if the Garou kill someone important.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052686-garou-and-vampires?p=1098673#post1098673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ghosts are the most numerous supernatural. Probably followed by Numinaed types(Hedge mages, psychics), Changelings have a much larger organization so they SEEM to have much higher numbers. Hell Ghouls/Kinfolk probably out number their respective big splat</div> </div> </div> </div>On Earth? Questionable.<br /> <br /> Also, as a longtime Changeling player, I was even thanked in one of the books, Changelings are a dying breed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-31T08:09:06-07:00","id":1098771,"title":"","content":"Wraiths seem to be around 1:20, Numinaed may be 1:500 to 1:5,000 (depending on the preference of the ST), Kithain seem to be 1:20,000 (when you add in the rest of the Changelings though, the Changeling population ratio could be as high as 1:5,000), Mages seem to be around 1:50,000 to 1:500,000 (depending on the edition), Kindred seem to be 1:50,000 to 1:100,000, and Garou seem to be 1:250,000 to 1:500,000. While Garou are not the rarest supernatural creature, they are pretty rare by any definition, so I do not buy the argument that they are one of the most numerous supernatural creatures (heck, they are not even the most numerous Fera, as the Ananasi and Ratkin both exceed the population of Garou on Earth).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-31T08:29:36-07:00","id":1098779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052686-garou-and-vampires?p=1098770#post1098770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A prince who just lets Garou act with impunity is going to lose his position very quickly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really, does a governor loose their job when a tornado blows through the state and tears things up?<br /> <br /> A Princes sole &quot;job&quot; is to enforce the traditions and I don't see any that require them to hunt werewolves.<br /> <br /> If anything the werewolves do the prince a service of eliminating troublesome vampires in their domain.<br /> <br /> BTW still waiting on what that world ending vampire win looks like.....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13009,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","user":"BurritoMage","date":". 05-31-2017, 12:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-31T09:03:33-07:00","id":1098792,"title":"","content":"Every other Kindred being killed and every other supernatural creature thinking that Kindred are extinct? It would be the of the world for the Kindred species...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-31T12:24:50-07:00","id":1098840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052686-garou-and-vampires?p=1098770#post1098770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Especially if the Garou kill someone important.</div> </div> </div> </div>This I could see leading to a hunt of sorts. Though the chances of actually getting the particular Garou responsible may or may not be likely depending on circumstance. This really would be more about the Vampire sending a message than actual effective revenge.<br /> The problem in general (from both splat's sides) is that they don't really know where to find the other one. Vampires tromping en masse out into the woods to teach those Lupines a lesson is going to go poorly. Same for Garou just randomly rampaging through a city.<br /> I could see a Prince attempting to pick off a few Garou (maybe even just one) and stringing them up their corpse(s) in court. Though even that is symbolic more than anything since 99% of Garou corpses are going to look like normal bodies. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052686-garou-and-vampires?p=1098770#post1098770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Also, as a longtime Changeling player, I was even thanked in one of the books, Changelings are a dying breed.</div> </div> </div> </div>So are Garou. Doesn't stop them from being relevant to the discussion at hand. And in theory, Changelings though dying do still far outnumber quite a bit of the Supernaturals in the WoD.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BurritoMage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052686-garou-and-vampires?p=1098779#post1098779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Not really, does a governor loose their job when a tornado blows through the state and tears things up?</div> </div> </div> </div>I really like this comparison. It seems particularly apt.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052686-garou-and-vampires?p=1098792#post1098792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Every other Kindred being killed and every other supernatural creature thinking that Kindred are extinct? It would be the of the world for the Kindred species...</div> </div> </div> </div>I think he/she was referring to a &quot;kindred win&quot; being the end of the world. It was from a post a page or 2 ago.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-31T12:49:08-07:00","id":1098849,"title":"","content":"I know, I was just suggesting individual 'Kindred win' scenarios because there is no 'Kindred win' end of the world scenario. Humans are required sustenance for Kindred (except for the practitioners of Bardo) and are the source of new Kindred. Even Kindred who loathe humans understand that they cannot exist without humans and that the massive overpopulation of the Kindred population would cause the end of the Kindred species as well as the end of humans (and any animal they could catch before they devolved into a permanent hunger frenzy after a few months without human blood).<br /> <br /> I am not really sure that a large Kindred population is a 'win' for any Kindred. Kindred are competitors for resources (blood, money, prestige, etc) in a way that humans really are not (Kindred can always blood bond, ghoul, or kill a human competitor that gets in the way). While organizations like the Camarilla are capable of regulating the competition between Kindred members to a certain degree, it does not eliminate it (it just makes it marginally less lethal and marginally more subtle). Even if Kindred want to avoid violating the conventions of the Camarilla by not killing off their Kindred competitors, they can 'temporarily' dispose of them for a few decades (or a few centuries) by staking them and burying them in a cement coffin in the foundation of a building. I imagine that quite a few Camarilla members are buried beneath the foundations of buildings, without a chance of being awakened until the building that traps them is demolished, when the Kindred who originally buried them will 'rescue' them and put them into a cement coffin beneath another building under construction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-31T14:50:46-07:00","id":1098906,"title":"","content":"If the Kindred eventually defeat all opponents, they will get devoured by their ancestors who will devour each other and destroy the world in the process. So, yeah, Gehenna is just another form of the Apocalypse. The Silent Striders along with the Union are the only supernaturals to have killed an Antediluvian so those other supernatural groups are the only possible salvation for the world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-31T15:13:33-07:00","id":1098913,"title":"","content":"Well, depending on your interpretation of events, 4th generation Kindred are capable of killing off 3rd generation Kindred.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-31T15:13:54-07:00","id":1098914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052686-garou-and-vampires?p=1098906#post1098906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the Kindred eventually defeat all opponents, they will get devoured by their ancestors who will devour each other and destroy the world in the process. So, yeah, Gehenna is just another form of the Apocalypse. The Silent Striders along with the Union are the only supernaturals to have killed an Antediluvian so those other supernatural groups are the only possible salvation for the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not how that works, that's not how any of this works. There is no set victory condition that triggers Gehenna, just like how there is no condition that triggers the Apocalypse.<br /> <br /> Even if the antediluvians woke up and proceeded to Murad the countryside like a bad Japanese monster film mortal militaries would have no problem taking care of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13009,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","user":"BurritoMage","date":". 05-31-2017, 06:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-31T15:42:11-07:00","id":1098921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BurritoMage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052686-garou-and-vampires?p=1098914#post1098914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's not how that works, that's not how any of this works. There is no set victory condition that triggers Gehenna, just like how there is no condition that triggers the Apocalypse.<br /> <br /> Even if the antediluvians woke up and proceeded to Murad the countryside like a bad Japanese monster film mortal militaries would have no problem taking care of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not really how the World of Darkness works.<br /> <br /> Is the world getting worse in RL?<br /> <br /> No.<br /> <br /> Is the world getting worse in the WoD?<br /> <br /> Yes.<br /> <br /> I think the other supernatural factions might have a chance against the Clan Founders in an integrated WOD. Humanity? No. Not a chance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 05-31-2017, 06:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-31T15:56:41-07:00","id":1098924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052686-garou-and-vampires?p=1098921#post1098921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the other supernatural factions might have a chance against the Clan Founders in an integrated WOD. Humanity? No. Not a chance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right because things that are cursed to burn in the sun are immune to atomic weapons.....<br /> <br /> If humanity was so weak why does each splat have a law in place to hide from it with steep penalties in some cases. <br /> <br /> Furthermore in the apocalypse book there is no scenario where the ancients rise up and only the supernatural super friends can defeat them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-31T18:38:57-07:00","id":1098959,"title":"","content":"Not immune to atomic weaponry? You mean like the Ravnos Antediluvian? Which was nuked <i>repeatedly</i>, before SUNLIGHT finally killed it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-31T18:49:03-07:00","id":1098963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BurritoMage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052686-garou-and-vampires?p=1098924#post1098924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Right because things that are cursed to burn in the sun are immune to atomic weapons.....</div> </div> </div> </div>It won't be Ventrue who kills you when Ventrue rises. It will be every soldier in the United States rounding up their fellow citizens, families, and children to be fed on blood altars. Because it's not the story of humanitys' triumph over evil but the story of monsters over humanity during the End of the World. People will line up for the privilege of being embraced so they can be diablerized because that's the way the Level 10 &quot;I win&quot; powers work without something equivalent to oppose them.<br /> <br /> Like, say, the Garou or Mages or Hunters.<br /> <br /> The Silent Striders killed Set, which is why the Garou are the best chance humanity has against them because the Antes got nothing on the Wyrm's worst.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If humanity was so weak why does each splat have a law in place to hide from it with steep penalties in some cases. </div> </div> </div>Middle-management is something humanity can handle. We're not prepared for handling the Eater-of-Souls or whatever the hell else is out in the Umbra. We HAVE humans who can defend the world against the Spirit World's worst.<br /> <br /> They're called Garou.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Furthermore in the apocalypse book there is no scenario where the ancients rise up and only the supernatural super friends can defeat them. </div> </div> </div>Um, gurahl****.<br /> <br /> Every single plot is about the Garou saving the world from the Wyrm or abandoning Earth. What exactly is the scenario where humans purify the Uncorrupted Metis' soul or free Anansi?<br /> <br /> The Garou are the heroes in Werewolf.<br /> <br /> Is there any scenario humans actually win against the supes?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 05-31-2017, 09:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-31T18:52:10-07:00","id":1098966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052686-garou-and-vampires?p=1098959#post1098959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not immune to atomic weaponry? You mean like the Ravnos Antediluvian? Which was nuked <i>repeatedly</i>, before SUNLIGHT finally killed it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically &quot;magical&quot; neutron bombs (which are still a theory at this point), which killed everything &quot;living&quot; to dispel the rain storm so the sunlight could finish it off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-31T18:57:56-07:00","id":1098968,"title":"","content":"The Fera (not just the Garou) are the Heroes of cWoD. The Wraiths are echoes of life, the Kindred are parasites, the KJ are fallen kings, the Changelings are dying gods, and the Mages are munchkins. Love them or hate them, the Fera are the thin furry line between humanity and annihilation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-31T18:58:45-07:00","id":1098970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052686-garou-and-vampires?p=1098963#post1098963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Garou are the heroes in Werewolf.</div> </div> </div> </div>So then why are you having a distinctly non werewolf antagonist be the end all of the werewolf setting?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052686-garou-and-vampires?p=1098968#post1098968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Love them or hate them, the Fera are the thin furry line between humanity and annihilation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, just forget the whole impergium part......","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13009,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","user":"BurritoMage","date":". 05-31-2017, 10:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-31T20:37:03-07:00","id":1099006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BurritoMage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052686-garou-and-vampires?p=1098970#post1098970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So then why are you having a distinctly non werewolf antagonist be the end all of the werewolf setting?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because people asked what a vampire victory would be like?<br /> <br /> Duh.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yeah, just forget the whole impergium part...... </div> </div> </div>Garou are awful at their job but it is their job.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-31T20:53:16-07:00","id":1099008,"title":"","content":"The Impergium stopped nine thousand years ago. It is not it is recent history.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-31T20:56:06-07:00","id":1099009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052686-garou-and-vampires?p=1099008#post1099008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Impergium stopped nine thousand years ago. It is not it is recent history.</div> </div> </div> </div> Not if you ask the red talons.....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-31T21:03:45-07:00","id":1099010,"title":"","content":"The Red Talons are a near extinct Tribe and, while they might want another Impergium, the other Garou have pretty much kept them in check. It happened nine thousand years ago (three hundred sixty generations ago), so it is hardly relevant. It did not even effect most of humanity (Sub-Saharan Africa, East Asia, Southeast Asia, North America, South America, and Australia were pretty much spared the Imperium from what I understand). You would be better off being pissed off about the Romans conquering Europe, that event occurred only two thousand years ago.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-31T22:26:29-07:00","id":1099025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052686-garou-and-vampires?p=1098770#post1098770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also, as a longtime Changeling player, I was even thanked in one of the books, Changelings are a dying breed.</div> </div> </div> </div>So are Fera. At various Times Khan have been called out as having only 50 in the world, Stargazers as having only 200 and Red Talons are called out as being worse off than this. So I'm going to stick with the elaborate feudal levels that Changeling society is able to function on puts them at more common than Werewolves. Its just Werewolves tend to Clump. You don't find them spread out there's lots of places they just don't exist. <br /> <br /> But where they exist its scary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-31T22:29:12-07:00","id":1099026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052686-garou-and-vampires?p=1099010#post1099010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Red Talons are a near extinct Tribe and, while they might want another Impergium, the other Garou have pretty much kept them in check. It happened nine thousand years ago (three hundred sixty generations ago), so it is hardly relevant. It did not even effect most of humanity (Sub-Saharan Africa, East Asia, Southeast Asia, North America, South America, and Australia were pretty much spared the Imperium from what I understand). You would be better off being pissed off about the Romans conquering Europe, that event occurred only two thousand years ago.</div> </div> </div> </div>If it's not such a big deal then why are humans still haunted by the delirium to this day?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-31T23:00:03-07:00","id":1099031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BurritoMage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052686-garou-and-vampires?p=1099026#post1099026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If it's not such a big deal then why are humans still haunted by the delirium to this day?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Same reason why the grim reaper is a multicultural thing, same reason most people are bothered by some form of insect. Some things get into the collective racial psyche and just don't really go away.<br /> <br /> Plus...9 foot tall slavering death machine. Most people in the real world have their little delusions to get them through the day and keep somewhat sane...pretty sure in the World of Darkness that goes double.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/690-fenris","name":"Fenris","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-01T06:21:53-07:00","id":1099129,"title":"","content":"Why do the Ananasi cause Delirium if they did not participate in the Impergium? It is because the Delirium is a psychological defense mechanism that protects individual mortals from acknowledging uncomfortable truths. Most mortals cannot accept that they are not the top dog.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-01T07:51:40-07:00","id":1099152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052686-garou-and-vampires?p=1099129#post1099129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why do the Ananasi cause Delirium if they did not participate in the Impergium? It is because the Delirium is a psychological defense mechanism that protects individual mortals from acknowledging uncomfortable truths. Most mortals cannot accept that they are not the top dog.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or because anyone would be terrified at the sight of them, which is what you get in situations where Nexus Crawlers materialize, or you see Godzilla stomping along the city. A living being, also a force of nature like a hurricane... or unnature, in the case of the Crawler.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-01T09:08:09-07:00","id":1099174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052686-garou-and-vampires?p=1099152#post1099152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Or because anyone would be terrified at the sight of them, which is what you get in situations where Nexus Crawlers materialize, or you see Godzilla stomping along the city. A living being, also a force of nature like a hurricane... or unnature, in the case of the Crawler.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> oh curious? do gifts that Reference or invoke the Delerium, work in &quot;war of the Dragon kings&quot; some explicitly cause it even in those normally immune.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-01T11:55:05-07:00","id":1099226,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052686-garou-and-vampires?p=1093672#post1093672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a 5th generation Kindred embraces two people every night, if the resulting 6th generation Kindred embraces two people every night, etc, one 5th generation Kindred can start a chain reaction that could convert an entire continent in a month.</div> </div> </div> </div> Sure, but that's an extremely unlikely scenario. It discounts any other variable such as people not following through on the chain, lack of people nearby, when people start fighting back, what happens when the Masquerade starts breaking, and lack of easy prey after a short order. Not to mention the plan isn't fully multiplicative after you reach a certain generation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052686-garou-and-vampires?p=1093738#post1093738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even if it is infeasible, the Garou still fear that sort of thing, as they do not want billions of superpowered fomori (in their interpretation) running around. Better for the Garou to kill the Kindred when they find them rather than let things explode out of control. The fact that the Anarchs and Sabbat bear most of the Garou attacks is a happy coincidence for the Cam and the Independents.</div> </div> </div> </div> Why would they fear something that's so rankly improbable? Do most Garou also fear interstellar space clowns from another universe as well? Certainly they don't want the Kindred to gain control or too strong, but this that they're afraid an entire continent is gonna get embrace is silly <i>because </i>of the fact it is so very unlikely.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","name":"Monalfie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12552_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-01T12:02:46-07:00","id":1099228,"title":"","content":"I am quite sure that the average Garou fears many of the things that come the Deep Umbra because they know some of what lurks in the Deep Umbra. If it happens to come in the form of circus clowns, the average Garou would probably not even bat an eye because that would not even be in the top thousand strangest things that the average Garou has seen. The chance of making it with Deep Umbra spirits in the form of female space clowns would probably be considered the best case scenario with any invasion from the Deep Umbra.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-01T12:12:27-07:00","id":1099231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052686-garou-and-vampires?p=1099228#post1099228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am quite sure that the average Garou fears many of the things that come the Deep Umbra because they know some of what lurks in the Deep Umbra. If it happens to come in the form of circus clowns, the average Garou would probably not even bat an eye because that would not even be in the top thousand strangest things that the average Garou has seen. The chance of making it with Deep Umbra spirits in the form of female space clowns would probably be considered the best case scenario with any invasion from the Deep Umbra.</div> </div> </div> </div> No, no. Now you are trying to change the scenario. Your claim was that Garou fear the likelihood of Kindred embracing an entire continent, despite it never happening and being extremely, extremely improbable. So for the scenario to be the same, you also think Garou are afraid of clowns that travel between universes, both something that doesn't really happen and extremely, extremely improbable. I'm not saying 'these things show up, the Garou worry'. But you seem to be claiming the Garou fear something that <i>could happen</i>, but will almost certainly never come to pass. They have actual things to worry about, like a Nexus Crawler, than making up absurd hypothetical scenarios.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","name":"Monalfie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12552_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-01T12:21:58-07:00","id":1099235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monalfie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052686-garou-and-vampires?p=1099226#post1099226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Do most Garou also fear interstellar space clowns from another universe as well?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Space clown phobia is actually the leading cause of Harano in my game.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-01T12:30:52-07:00","id":1099243,"title":"","content":"Garou hate vampires.<br /> <br /> Garou FEAR Space Cthulhu that eat continents.<br /> <br /> They know both exist.<br /> <br /> Also, Stephen King's &quot;It&quot; with Pennywise as a Deep Umbra Wyrm thing that takes over a town, corrupts the population, and gets eaten by a giant turtle at the end is not actually that far from what a Garou would think a fairly normal occurrence for them to deal with. About the only thing they'd have a problem with is the child-orgy and that's because Garou don't mate with other Garou.<br /> <br /> Werewolf gets a lot of focus on the environment business but they live in a Lovecraftian world. It just so happens they're Ghouls versus Humans.<br /> <br /> Mostly helpless rather than completely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 06-01-2017, 03:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-01T12:34:40-07:00","id":1099247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052686-garou-and-vampires?p=1099228#post1099228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am quite sure that the average Garou fears many of the things that come the Deep Umbra because they know some of what lurks in the Deep Umbra. If it happens to come in the form of circus clowns, the average Garou would probably not even bat an eye because that would not even be in the top thousand strangest things that the average Garou has seen. The chance of making it with Deep Umbra spirits in the form of female space clowns would probably be considered the best case scenario with any invasion from the Deep Umbra.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> But vampires are not creatures of the Deep Umbra, and in general don't play in the same part of the pool. Barring that random Garou Dudeman(or woman) walking around with Sense Wyrm active ALL the time, most Garou probably won't recognize Joe and Jane vampire unless they catch them playing with their food. Likewise, short of Joe and Jane vampire running across Garou in Crinos or big doggie form, they likely won't have a clue that they ran across a Garou, and if they do run across that, common sense for survival dictates not starting a fight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/690-fenris","name":"Fenris","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-01T12:50:31-07:00","id":1099250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052686-garou-and-vampires?p=1099243#post1099243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, Stephen King's &quot;It&quot; with Pennywise as a Deep Umbra Wyrm thing that takes over a town, corrupts the population, and gets eaten by a giant turtle at the end is not actually that far from what a Garou would think a fairly normal occurrence for them to deal with...<br /> <br /> Werewolf gets a lot of focus on the environment business but they live in a Lovecraftian world. It just so happens they're Ghouls versus Humans.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would not look to works like 'It' or Lovecraft's corpus to define Werewolf. There are some surface similarities between the Wyrm and the alien gods of the Mythos, but the underlying themes are fairly dissimilar. The inherent meaninglessness of life in the face of cosmic horror featured in Lovecraft's universe doesn't jive with Garou cosmology at all. The Wyrm is a disastrous, maddening evil, but you can fight against it. You must fight against it, as the Garou have done for centuries. Gaia (the soul of the world) is worth fighting for, and it may be possible, albeit with intense personal and societal sacrifice, to overcome the ultimate enemy.<br /> <br /> I think people that compare WtA to Lovecraft kinda miss the boat, and can't see the forest for the tentacles. Garou aren't Ghouls, the Wyrm isn't Yog-Sothoth or the Wyld Azathoth- nothing is closely analogous, and rightly so. Different stories, different messages. WtA has more heroism and less cosmic, otherworldly horror. When the horror does come, often it isn't existential terror, but rather personal sins committed due to unfettered rage or misplaced zealotry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3695,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","user":"The Laughing Stranger","date":". 06-01-2017, 04:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-01T13:01:26-07:00","id":1099252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fenris</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052686-garou-and-vampires?p=1099247#post1099247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> But vampires are not creatures of the Deep Umbra, and in general don't play in the same part of the pool. Barring that random Garou Dudeman(or woman) walking around with Sense Wyrm active ALL the time, most Garou probably won't recognize Joe and Jane vampire unless they catch them playing with their food. Likewise, short of Joe and Jane vampire running across Garou in Crinos or big doggie form, they likely won't have a clue that they ran across a Garou, and if they do run across that, common sense for survival dictates not starting a fight.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. Garou have better things to do than hunt Kindred unless they are being unsubtle or attacking their Kinfolk (or Mortal associates) and Kindred have better things to do than commit suicide by attacking Garou. Of course, the rarity of each group makes random encounters statistically improbable (Garou probably have a 1:50,000 chance that any mortal they encounter are actually Kindred and Kindred probably have a 1:50,000 chance that any mortal they encounter are actually Fera [10%-20% of whom would be Garou]).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-01T13:30:40-07:00","id":1099265,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052686-garou-and-vampires?p=1098963#post1098963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Silent Striders killed Set, which is why the Garou are the best chance humanity has against them because the Antes got nothing on the Wyrm's worst.</div> </div> </div> </div>IIRC, I don't think they destroyed Set. Although Shu Horus managed to fight him <i>to a draw</i> and live to walk away from it, which in and of itself qualifies for the list of Top Ten Most Badass Accomplishments in the World of Darkness Ever. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-01T13:34:31-07:00","id":1099268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052686-garou-and-vampires?p=1099265#post1099265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> IIRC, I don't think they destroyed Set. Although Shu Horus managed to fight him <i>to a draw</i> and live to walk away from it, which in and of itself qualifies for the list of Top Ten Most Badass Accomplishments in the World of Darkness Ever.</div> </div> </div> </div>Set is notably a dead Antediluvian. One of the few confirmed so as their Gehenna scenario is a magical ritual to bring him back.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-01T13:36:49-07:00","id":1099269,"title"